hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"12601","12567 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili narrated to us, Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Thabit ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas who said: I stood one night to pray with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and stood at his left; he signaled with his hand from behind me, taking my hand, or my upper arm, until he placed me at his right."
"12602","12568 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin and Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Wadih al-Assal, the two Egyptians, narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Sha'bi who said: I asked Abdullah ibn Abbas and Abdullah ibn Umar: How was the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They said: Thirteen: eight, he prays witr with three, and two after dawn."
"12603","12569 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: Say, I ask you no reward for it except love for kin: he said: That you maintain ties with my kin and do not belie me."
"12604","12570 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instituted the witr and the two units of travel."
"12605","12571 - Ali ibn al-Abbas al-Bajali al-Kufi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Subayh narrated to us, Nasr ibn Muzahim narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, when were you written as a prophet? He said: While Adam was between spirit and body."
"12606","12572 - Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq al-Marwazi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a shoulder of sheep in the mosque and ate it, then stood for prayer without touching water."
"12607","12573 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, Umar ibn Amir narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade taking anything with a soul as a target."
"12608","12574 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khallad ibn Yahya narrated to us (ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drinking standing from Zamzam - and the wording is that of the hadith of Abu Nu'aym."
"12609","12575 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought drink and we gave him of Zamzam; he drank while standing."
"12610","12576 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas who said: I handed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a bucket of Zamzam and he drank while standing."
"12611","12577 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought drink and was brought a bucket of Zamzam; he drank while standing."
"12612","12578 - Abu Urubah al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Harrani narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim al-Harrani narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Muslim, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas who said: I gave the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Zamzam to drink and he drank while standing."
"12613","12579 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Isbahani narrated to us (ha). And Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us; both said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas who said: I brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a bucket of Zamzam and he drank while standing."
"12614","12580 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a bier after it had been buried."
"12615","12581 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi who said: One who witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me: he came to an isolated grave, arranged them in rows and pronounced four takbirs. Sulayman said: I said to al-Sha'bi: O Abu Amr, who narrated this to you? He said: Ibn Abbas."
"12616","12582 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Amir, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a grave and said: What is this? They said: He or she was buried last night. Ibn Abbas said: So he lined us up behind him, then he prayed over her."
"12617","12583 - Ahmad ibn Ziyad ibn Zakariyya al-Iyadi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Qays narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Jafar ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a grave and said: What is this? They said: He was buried last night. Ibn Abbas said: So we lined up behind him, then he prayed over him."
"12618","12584 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped on the two jugular veins, and he gave the cupper his wage, and had it been unlawful he would not have given it to him."
"12619","12585 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for Abu Taybah, who cupped him, and he reduced half a sa or more from his Kharaj tax."
"12620","12586 - Abu Husayn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Jabir, from Amir, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be cupped three times on the two jugular veins and between the shoulders; a slave boy of his from Bayadah called Abu Hind used to cup him, and he used to pay his family a mudd and a half every day, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) interceded for him and they reduced half a mudd from him, and afterwards the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give the cupper his wage, and had it been unlawful he would not have given it to him."
"12621","12587 - Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped on the two jugular veins and the upper back."
"12622","12588 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us, Sharik and Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be cupped on the two jugular veins and the upper back."
"12623","12589 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Khalid al-Shairi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Rabah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mamar, from Asim from Sulayman, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped; a freed slave of Banu Bayadah cupped him, and he gave him his wage, and had it been unlawful he would not have given it to him."
"12624","12590 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Sumay al-Zayyat, from Ibn Abbas who said: I stood beside the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his left, so he turned me and placed me on his right."
"12625","12591 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Khalid ibn Tahman Abu al-Ala al-Khaffaf narrated to us, from Husayn who said: A beggar asked while Ibn Abbas was in prayer, so Ibn Abbas said to him: O beggar. He said: At your service. He said: Do you testify that there is no god but Allah? He said: Yes. He said: And do you pray the five prayers? He said: Yes. He said: And do you fast Ramadan? He said: Yes. He said: It is binding on us to maintain ties with you, so he removed a garment he was wearing and clothed him with it, then he said at that: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any Muslim who clothes a Muslim with a garment remains under the protection of Allah as long as a patch of it remains on him."
"12626","12592 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Awf al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Kamil Abu al-Ala, from Husayn, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"12627","12593 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Kathir ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun who said: We were with Ibn Abbas when seven men came to him while he was then healthy, before he went blind, and they said: O Ibn Abbas, come with us, or he said: Leave, O you people. He said: Rather I will come with you. So he stood with them, and we do not know what they said. Then he returned dusting his garment and saying: Uff, uff, they attacked a man concerning whom I will tell you now what was said about him; they attacked Ali ibn Abi Talib. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall surely send a man whom Allah will not disgrace. So he sent for Ali while he was grinding at the millstone, which none of you would grind, and they brought him with sore eyes. He said: O Prophet of Allah, I can hardly see. So he spat in his eyes and shook the banner three times, then handed it to him, and victory was granted to him, and he brought Safiyyah bint Huyayy. Then he said to his cousins three times: Which of you will be my ally in this world and the Hereafter, until he passed the last of them, then Ali said: O Prophet of Allah, I am your ally in this world and the Hereafter. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are my ally in this world and the Hereafter. He said: And he sent Abu Bakr with Surah al-Tawbah, and sent Ali after him. Abu Bakr said: O Ali, perhaps Allah and His Prophet are angry with me. Ali said: No, but the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting that any but a man from me should convey from me, and I am from him. He said: And the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his cloak over Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan and al-Husayn, and said: Allah only wishes to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly. And he was the first to accept Islam after Khadijah among the people. He said: And Ali sold himself; he wore the garment of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then stood in his place. The polytheists were pelting the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with stones, then Abu Bakr came and said: Come to me, O Messenger of Allah, while Abu Bakr thought he was the Prophet of Allah. Ali said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has set out toward the well of Maymun, so catch up with him. So Abu Bakr set out and entered the cave with him. And Ali kept throwing stones as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to throw, writhing, having wrapped his head in the garment without bringing it out until morning. Then he uncovered his head in the morning, and they said: You are indeed ungenerous; we used to pelt your companion with stones and he would not writhe, while you writhe, and we found that strange. He said: Then he went out with the people on the Tabuk expedition, and Ali said to him: Shall I go out with you? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: No. So Ali wept, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Are you not pleased to be to me as Harun was to Musa, except that you are not a prophet; it is not fitting that I go except with you as my successor. He said: And he said to him: You are the ally of every believer after me. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) closed the doors of the mosque except the door of Ali, so he would enter the mosque in a state of major impurity while it was his passage, having no other passage. He said: And he said: Whomsoever I am his master, Ali is his master. Ibn Abbas said: Allah informed us in the Quran that He was pleased with them, the companions of the Tree, knowing what was in their hearts, so did He ever tell us that He became angry with them afterwards? And he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umar when he said: Will you permit me to strike his neck, meaning Hatib: Would you have done it? And what do you know; perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do as you wish?"
"12628","12594 - Abu Shuayb Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered all the doors to be shut except the door of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
"12629","12595 - Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari and Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Turki narrated to us, they said: Ubaydullah ibn Aishah narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man from Banu Amir came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he used to treat and heal, and he said: O Muhammad, you say things; shall I treat you? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invited him to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, then said: Shall I show you a sign? And near him were palms and a tree, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called a cluster from it, and it came toward him, prostrating and raising its head, until it reached him and stood before him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to it: Return to your place. So it returned to its place. The Amiri said: By Allah, I shall never belie you in any saying, then he said: O family of Banu Sasah, by Allah, I shall never belie him in anything he says."
"12630","12596 - Muhammad ibn al-Faraj al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: I found in my book, from Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali, from al-Sabbah ibn Yahya al-Muzani, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Ibn Abbas who said: While we were washing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man came and knocked at the door and said: I remind you of Allah; grant me today a share of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ali said: Admit him, and place him behind the curtain to hand us water. So we admitted him, and he used to hand us water. And Ali said: By Allah, I never turned him over but another was with me turning him over. He said: And I heard in the house: Do not remove the shirt from him."
"12631","12597 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Mutahhar ibn al-Hakam al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from his father, he said: Layth ibn Abi Sulaym informed me, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad who said: I was sitting with Abdullah ibn Abbas when a man came to him and said: What do you think of one who kills a believer intentionally, then repents, believes, does righteous deeds, then is guided? He said: And how can he repent, when I heard your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The nearest of creatures to the Throne of the Most Merciful on the Day of Resurrection is the believer who was killed wrongfully, with his head in his right hand and his killer on his left, his jugular veins gushing, saying: My Lord, ask this one for what he killed me; for what did he bar me from prayer?"
"12632","12598 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Israel informed us, from Ali ibn Badhimah, from Qays ibn Habtar, from Ibn Abbas, that he was asked about the earthen jar, and he said: The first to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about nabidh were Abd al-Qays; they came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a fertile land, and we get produce, so command us a drink. He said: Make nabidh in waterskins, and do not make nabidh in the earthen jar, nor the gourd, nor the tarred vessel, nor the hollowed stump, for I have been forbidden wine, gambling, the kuba, which is the drum, and every intoxicant is unlawful. They said: O Messenger of Allah, if it becomes strong? He said: Pour water on it. They said: O Messenger of Allah, if it becomes strong? He said: Pour water on it. He said on the third or fourth time: If it becomes strong, then spill it."
"12633","12599 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Ali ibn Badhimah, from Qays ibn Habtar, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of the hadith of Israel."
"12634","12600 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Ali ibn Mabad narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Ali ibn Badhimah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Qays ibn Habtar, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is unlawful."
"12635","12601 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Said ibn Hafs al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: We read to Ubaydullah ibn Miqal, from Abd al-Karim, from Qays ibn Habtar al-Rabai, from Abdullah ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The price of wine is unlawful, the wage of the prostitute is unlawful, the price of the dog is unlawful, the kuba is unlawful, and if the owner of the dog comes to you, fill his hands with dust; wine, gambling and every intoxicant are unlawful."
"12636","12602 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Bishr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr who said: Ibn Abbas said to me: Which of the two readings do you recite? I said: The last one. He said: Jibril, peace be upon him, used to present the Quran to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) every year in Ramadan. He said: So he presented the Quran to him twice in the year in which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away. So Abdullah witnessed what was abrogated of it and what was changed, and Abdullah recited the last reading."
"12637","12603 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Abi Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: Then he was at a distance of two bows or nearer, who said: The qab is the fetter, and the two bows are the two forearms."
"12638","12604 - al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abayah ibn Ribi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah divided creation into two groups and placed me in the better of the two groups, the companions of the right, and I am the best of the companions of the right. Then He made the two groups into houses and placed me in the better of the two houses, and that is His saying: Then the companions of the right, what are the companions of the right, and the companions of the left, what are the companions of the left, and the foremost, the foremost. So I am among the best of the foremost. Then He made the house into tribes and placed me in the best tribe, and that is His saying: peoples and tribes, the verse. So I am the most God-fearing of the children of Adam and the noblest of them to Allah, and no boast. Then He made the tribes into houses and placed me in the best house. So that is His saying: Allah only wishes to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly."
"12639","12605 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Said ibn Amr ibn Said al-Qurashi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What deed, if I do it, will admit me to Paradise? He said: Are you in a land where water is brought? He said: Yes. He said: Then buy a new waterskin there, then draw water in it until you wear it out, for you will not wear it out until you attain thereby the deed of Paradise."
"12640","12606 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us. And Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Wakii narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, they said: Isa ibn Sawadah Abu al-Sabbah al-Nakhai narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Zadham who said: Ibn Abbas fell ill with a grave illness, so he gathered his sons and family to him and said to them: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever performs Hajj from Makkah on foot until he returns to it, for him is seven hundred good deeds of the good deeds of the sanctuary for every step. Some of them said: And what are the good deeds of the sanctuary? He said: Every good deed therein is a thousand good deeds."
"12641","12607 - Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Zimmi narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Sumay al-Hanafi, from Abu Malik al-Ghifari, from Ibn Abbas who said: This verse was revealed: And do not marry polytheist women until they believe. So people refrained from them until the one after it was revealed: This day the good things have been made lawful for you, and the food of those given the Book is lawful for you, and your food is lawful for them, and the chaste women of the believers and the chaste women of those given the Book. So people married the women of the People of the Book."
"12642","12608 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Good conduct and good demeanor are a part of seventy parts of prophethood."
"12643","12609 - Abu Amir Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Nahwi al-Suri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Uthman ibn Faid narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good conduct, good demeanor and moderation are a part of forty-five parts of prophethood."
"12644","12610 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Qabus narrated to us, that his father narrated to him, he said: We said to Ibn Abbas: What do you think of the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: Allah has not made for any man two hearts in his breast? He said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood one day praying and a passing thought occurred, so the hypocrites who prayed with him said: Do you not see that he has two hearts, a heart with you and a heart with them? So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: Allah has not made for any man two hearts in his breast."
"12645","12611 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: Two men with one need came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); one of them greeted, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found a bad smell from his mouth, so he said to him: Do you not use the tooth-stick? He said: I do, but I have not tasted food for three days. So he ordered a man to host him and fulfill his need."
"12646","12612 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim al-Jawhari narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who plunders, robs, or points to robbery."
"12647","12613 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he passed by the graves in Madinah and said: Peace be upon you, O people of the graves, believers and Muslims; I ask Allahs forgiveness for us and for you; you are our predecessors, and we follow after."
"12648","12614 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, from Qabus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The women said: O Messenger of Allah, why does he mention the believing men and not mention the believing women? So there was revealed: Indeed the Muslim men and Muslim women, and the believing men and believing women."
"12649","12615 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Basri narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) part the thighs of al-Husayn and kiss his small member."
"12650","12616 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the owner of begging knew what is in it for him, he would not beg."
"12651","12617 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Layth narrated to us, al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas: And if there were a Quran by which the mountains were moved, or the earth cut apart, or the dead spoken to, he said: They said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If it is as you say, show us our first elders among the dead to speak to them, and open for us these mountains, the mountains of Makkah which have hemmed us in. So there was revealed: And if there were a Quran by which the mountains were moved, or the earth cut apart, or the dead spoken to."
"12652","12618 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Layth narrated to us, al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Qabus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, My Lord, admit me with an entry of truth and bring me out with an exit of truth, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained ten years in Makkah, then there was revealed: And say: My Lord, admit me with an entry of truth and bring me out with an exit of truth. So he migrated to Madinah."
"12653","12619 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The man in whose breast there is nothing of the Quran is like the ruined house."
"12654","12620 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none among you but that his companion from the devils has been assigned to him. They said: And you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, but Allah helped me against him, so he submitted."
"12655","12621 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us hurrying while we were seated, and his haste startled us. When he reached us he greeted, then said: I came to you hurrying to inform you of the Night of Decree, then I forgot it on the way to you, so seek it in the last ten nights."
"12656","12622 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, they said: Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abu Zibyan, from Ibn Abbas who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: By what shall I know that you are the Messenger of Allah? He said: If I call this cluster from this palm, will you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. So the cluster came down from the palm until it fell to the ground, then it hopped until it came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he said to it: Return. So it returned until it went back to its place. So he said: I testify that you are the Messenger of Allah, and he believed."
"12657","12623 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us, my uncle Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abu Muslim Qaid al-Amash narrated to us, from Yahya Abu Umar, from Ibn Abbas who said: Raisins used to be soaked for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) overnight, and he would drink it the next day and its night, and the next day and its night, and the next day, until when evening came he drank it or gave it to drink, or ordered it to be spilled."
"12658","12624 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Umar, from Ibn Abbas who said: Raisins used to be soaked for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would drink it that day and the next, and after the next until the evening of its night, then he would order it to be given to drink or spilled."
"12659","12625 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Yahya ibn Ubayd al-Bahrani, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to have nabidh made for him, and he would drink it the next day and after the next; when it was the third day he ordered it to be spilled."
"12660","12626 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Yahya ibn Ubayd, from Ibn Abbas, the like of it."
"12661","12627 - Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Ayyub al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Said ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to us, Abu Tumaylah Yahya ibn Wadih narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Jabir, from Yahya ibn Ubayd Abu Umar, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to have raisins soaked for him in a waterskin, and he would drink it from the evening, and the next day and after the next; if any remained he ordered it to be spilled or drunk."
"12662","12628 - al-Husayn ibn Mansur al-Rummani al-Massisi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Muadh narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Abu Amr ibn al-Ala, from Muhammad ibn Abi Layla, from Yahya ibn Ubayd al-Bahrani, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to have nabidh made for him, and he would drink it during the day and its night, and the next day and its night; when it was the third day he ordered it to be spilled or given to the servants to drink."
"12663","12629 - Mahmud ibn al-Faraj al-Asbahani narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Jafar ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muti al-Ghazzal, from Yahya ibn Ubayd al-Bahrani, from Ibn Abbas who said: Nabidh used to be made for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a waterskin, and he would drink it the next day and its night, and the next day and its night; when it was the third he ordered it to be spilled or gave it to the servants to drink."
"12664","12630 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl al-Nakhai narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Ubayd al-Bahrani, from Ibn Abbas who said: Drink used to be soaked for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would drink it on its day, and the next day, and the third day; when evening came he spilled it or gave it to the servants to drink, and he did not give the servants anything unlawful to drink."
"12665","12631 - Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Abu Israil al-Mulai narrated to us, from Abu Umar, from Ibn Abbas who said: Nabidh used to be made for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would drink it the next day and after the next; when the evening of the third day came he spilled it or ordered it to be spilled."
"12666","12632 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us. And Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ubayd who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the gourd, the green jar, and the hollowed stump."
"12667","12633 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hawwas al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Yahya Abu Umar, from Ibn Abbas who said: Wine was prohibited in itself, its little and its much, and intoxication from every drink."
"12668","12634 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Arqam ibn Shurahbil who said: I travelled with Ibn Abbas from Madinah to Sham, and I asked him: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) make a will? He said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill with the illness in which he died, he was in the house of Aishah. He said: Call Ali for me. She said: Shall we not call Abu Bakr, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Call him. Then Hafsah said: Shall we not call Umar? He said: Call him. Then Umm al-Fadl said: Shall we not call al-Abbas, your uncle? He said: Call him. When they were present he raised his head and did not see Ali, so he remained silent and did not speak. Umar said: Leave the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); if he had any need of us he would have mentioned it. He did that three times. Then he said: Let Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer. Aishah said: Abu Bakr was present, so Abu Bakr stepped forward leading the people in prayer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt some relief, so he went out supported between two men. When the people sensed him they glorified Allah, and Abu Bakr went to step back, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) signalled to him: Stay in your place. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began from where Abu Bakr had reached in the recitation, with Abu Bakr standing and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sitting; Abu Bakr followed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the people followed Abu Bakr. No sooner had the Messenger of Allah finished the prayer than he became very heavy, and he went out supported between two men, his feet trailing on the ground. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died without making a will."
"12669","12635 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abu Janab al-Kalbi, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has enough to reach the Sacred House of Allah for Hajj but does not perform Hajj, and whoever has wealth reaching zakat but does not pay zakat, will ask to return at death. A man said to him: Fear Allah, O Abu Abbas; only the disbeliever asks to return. He said: I shall recite Quran to you: O you who believe, and spend of what We have provided you before death comes to one of you and he says: My Lord, if only You would delay me for a near term."
"12670","12636 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Hayyah Abu Janab, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has enough to perform Hajj but does not perform Hajj, or has what he must pay zakat on but does not pay it, will ask to return at death. A man said to him: Fear Allah, O Abu Abbas; only the disbeliever asks to return. He said: I shall recite Quran to you: O you who believe, and spend of what We have provided you before death comes to one of you and he says: My Lord, if only You would delay me for a near term, so I would give charity and be among the righteous."
"12671","12637 - al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Basri al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Abi al-Waddah narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, Razin al-Jurjani narrated to me, he said: I asked Said ibn Jubayr about this verse: And married women, and he said: I have no knowledge of it. So I asked al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, mentioning the saying of Said ibn Jubayr, and he said: I bear witness I heard him asking Ibn Abbas about it, and Ibn Abbas said: It was revealed on the day of Khaybar, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered it; the Muslims took among the women of the People of the Book those with husbands. When a man wished to approach one of them she would say: I have a husband. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about that, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed this verse: And married women, the verse, meaning the captive from the polytheists when taken, there is no harm in that. So I mentioned that to Said ibn Jubayr, and he said: He spoke the truth."
"12672","12638 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Abd al-Salam ibn Nahshal, a man kunya Abu Abdullah narrated to me, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Goodness comes more swiftly to the house in which food is served than the knife to the hump of the camel."
"12673","12639 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, dictated from his original book, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Umar Abu Yahya, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing every living soul except if it harms."
"12674","12640 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Abu Awanah informed us, from Abu Sinan, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas concerning the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: When the Prophet confided a report to one of his wives, who said: Hafsah entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in her house while he was intimate with Mariyah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Do not inform Aishah until I give you glad tidings: your father will rule after Abu Bakr when I die. So Hafsah went and told Aishah that she had seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intimate with Mariyah, and told her that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had informed her that Abu Bakr would rule after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Umar after him. Aishah said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Who informed you of this? He said: The All-Knowing, the All-Aware informed me. Aishah said: I shall not look at you until you forbid Mariyah to yourself. So he forbade her, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: O Prophet, why do you forbid."
"12675","12641 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafii narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One killed defending his wealth is a martyr, one killed defending his family is a martyr, and one killed defending himself is a martyr."
"12676","12642 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqal al-Harrani narrated to us, al-Nufayli narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the like of it exactly."
"12677","12643 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Said Abu Sad al-Baqqal, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beautify your voices with the Quran."
"12678","12644 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Mirdas al-Ansari narrated to us, Jariyah ibn Harim narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr with Asr, and Maghrib with Isha, in Madinah without excuse. It was said to Ibn Abbas: What did he intend by that? He said: Ease for his community."
"12679","12645 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs ibn Ibrahim al-Ansari al-Balkhi narrated to us, Asram ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Qurrah ibn Khalid and Abu Abdullah al-Qushayri, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Today is the wagering, tomorrow is the race, and the goal is Paradise or Hell; I am first, Abu Bakr the second, Umar third, and the people after according to precedence, the first then the first."
"12680","12646 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Yahya ibn Kathir Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, when was your covenant taken? He said: While Adam was between spirit and body."
"12681","12647 - Ubayd ibn Kathir al-Tammar narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, from Nahshal ibn Said, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None has conferred more favor on me with his hand than Abu Bakr; he married his daughter to me and brought me out to the land of migration. Had I taken a close friend I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but brotherhood and affection until the Day of Resurrection."
"12682","12648 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas who said: I was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a donkey called Yafur, and I sweated, so he ordered me to wash."
"12683","12649 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas who said: Whenever Jibril, peace be upon him, brought revelation to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would not finish until he was wrapped up from the revelation; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would speak its beginning fearing he would be overcome, so Jibril said to him: Why do you do that? He said: Fearing I may forget. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: We shall teach you, so you will not forget."
"12684","12650 - al-Muntasir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Hammad Sajjadah narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, conversed with Musa in one hundred and forty thousand words over three days. When Musa, peace be upon him, heard the speech of human beings he despised them because of what had fallen upon his hearing of the speech of the Lord, Mighty and Majestic. Among what He conversed with him was His saying: O Musa, the pretentious have not feigned with the like of asceticism in this world, those who draw near to Me have not drawn near with the like of piety from what I forbade them, and worshippers have not worshipped with the like of weeping from fear of Me. Musa said: O Lord of all creatures, O Master of the Day of Judgment, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor, what have You prepared for them, and what have You rewarded them? He said: As for the ascetics in this world, I shall grant them My Paradise to dwell wherever they wish. As for the God-fearing from what I forbade them, when the Day of Resurrection comes there will remain no servant but I shall scrutinize his reckoning except the God-fearing, for I shall be shy of them, honor them, dignify them, and admit them to Paradise without reckoning. As for those who weep from fear of Me, theirs is the highest eminence, unshared therein."
"12685","12651 - Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Hammad al-Barbari narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one killed in the path of Allah advancing, not retreating, precedes the slain retreating to Paradise by seventy autumns, and the sick of my community precede their healthy by seventy autumns, and the prophets precede Sulayman ibn Dawud by forty autumns because of the kingship he had."
"12686","12652 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman shall not travel three miles except with a husband or a mahram. It was said to Ibn Abbas: People say three days. He said: That is only a mistake of theirs."
"12687","12653 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tied the banner for Ali on the day of Khaybar, he supplicated for him a while, saying: O Allah, help him, honor through him, have mercy on him and have mercy through him, grant him victory and grant victory through him. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, and oppose whoever opposes him."
"12688","12654 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Bishr ibn Umarah narrated to us, from Abu Rawq, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wished to go out to the Tabuk expedition, he said to al-Jadd ibn Qays: O Jadd ibn Qays, what do you say about striving against Banu al-Asfar? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man fond of women; when I see the women of Banu al-Asfar I shall be tempted, so permit me to stay and do not tempt me. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: Among them is he who says: Permit me and do not tempt me; unquestionably, into temptation they have fallen."
"12689","12655 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Awn ibn Sallam narrated to us, Bishr ibn Umarah narrated to us, from Abu Rawq, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: He will appoint for them affection, who said: Love in the breasts of the believers, revealed concerning Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah honor his face."
"12690","12656 - Ahmad ibn Zakariyya Shadhan al-Basri narrated to us, Kathir ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abu Rawq, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No moderate person ever became poor."
"12691","12657 - Ahmad ibn Zakariyya Shadhan narrated to us, Kathir ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Qasri narrated to us, from Abu Rawq, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are two veils: the husband and the grave."
"12692","12658 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Bishr ibn Umarah narrated to us, from Abu Rawq, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: For they do not belie you, unaccented, and so he used to recite it, who said: They cannot make him not a messenger, nor make the Quran not the Quran; as for belying you with their tongues, they do belie you, and that is but falsehood, and that is the belying."
"12693","12659 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Bishr ibn Umarah narrated to us, from Abu Rawq, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: Do not say raina, who said: They used to say to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Lend us your hearing, for raina is like your saying: grant us. And hear without being heard, to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: They say: May you not hear; and hear, to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): May you not hear. He said: Had they said: We hear and obey, and hear and look upon us, it would have been better for them."
"12694","12660 - Abu Umar al-Darir Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Warqa, from Nahshal ibn Said, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition and they gained spoils, he took a fifth of the spoils and divided that fifth into five, then recited: And know that whatever you gain, a fifth of it is for Allah, to His saying: Allah is the key of speech, To Allah belongs what is in the heavens and the earth. So he made the share of Allah and the share of the Messenger one, and for near kin, so he made these two shares as strength in horses and weapons, and he made the share of orphans, the poor and the traveler to be given to none but them, and he made the remaining four shares: two shares for the horse, one share for its rider, and one share for the foot soldier."
"12695","12661 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us. And Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Hamid ibn al-Hasan al-Hilali narrated to us, from Nahshal ibn Said, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Safety for my community from drowning when they board ships is to say: In the name of Allah the King, And they did not esteem Allah as He deserves, and the earth entirely is His grasp on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens folded in His right hand; glory be to Him, exalted above what they associate, In the name of Allah is its course and its anchorage; indeed my Lord is Forgiving, Merciful."
"12696","12662 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sarraj al-Askari narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjumanî narrated to us, Sad ibn Said al-Jurjani narrated to us, from Nahshal Abu Abdullah al-Rasibi, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The nobles of my community are the bearers of the Quran."
"12697","12663 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, Zaidah ibn Umayr al-Tai narrated to us, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: What do you think about withdrawal? He said: If the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said anything about it, it is as he said; otherwise I say about it: Your women are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish. Whoever wishes may practice withdrawal, and whoever wishes may leave it."
"12698","12664 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr al-Amidi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Zaidah ibn Umayr who said: I asked Ibn Abbas about prayer while travelling, and he said: Two rakahs, two rakahs, the practice of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12699","12665 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, they said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, al-Agharr ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, from Khalifah ibn Husayn, from Abu Nasr al-Asadi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hesitated over a verse in the dawn prayer; when he finished the prayer he turned to the people with his face and said: Did Ubayy ibn Kab attend the prayer with you? They said: No. He said: So the people thought he missed him only to have him correct him."
"12700","12666 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from al-Agharr ibn al-Sabbah, from Khalifah ibn Husayn, from Abu Nasr, from Ibn Abbas who said: Aws and Khazraj in the pre-Islamic age had evil between them. One day while they were sitting they recalled what was between them until they became angry, and some of them rose against others with weapons. So there was revealed: How can you disbelieve while the verses of Allah are recited to you and His Messenger is among you, the whole verse, and the two verses after it, up to: And remember the favor of Allah upon you when you were enemies and He united your hearts."
"12701","12667 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Layth narrated to me, al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Agharr ibn al-Sabbah, from Khalifah ibn Husayn, from Abu Nasr, from Ibn Abbas: How can you disbelieve while the verses of Allah are recited to you and His Messenger is among you, he said: Aws were talking when they recalled the affair of the pre-Islamic age, and they became angry until there was war between them; they took weapons and some walked toward others. So there was revealed: How can you disbelieve while the verses of Allah are recited to you, up to His saying: So He saved you from it."
"12702","12668 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from al-Agharr ibn al-Sabbah, from Khalifah ibn Husayn, from Abu Nasr who said: Ibn Abbas was asked: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) test the women? He said: When a woman came to him to accept Islam, he would make her swear by Allah that she had not gone out from hatred of a husband, and by Allah that she had not gone out to earn a dinar, and by Allah that she had not gone out desiring one land over another, and by Allah that she had not gone out except from love of Allah and His Messenger."
"12703","12669 - Ali ibn al-Abbas al-Bajali al-Kufi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from al-Agharr ibn al-Sabbah, from Khalifah ibn Husayn, from Abu Nasr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed three umrahs in Dhu al-Qadah."
"12704","12670 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from Atiyyah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How can I enjoy when the keeper of the Trumpet has taken the Trumpet? And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed his forehead, awaiting when he would be commanded to blow. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall we say? He said: Allah suffices us, and He is the best Disposer. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: When the Trumpet is blown."
"12705","12671 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Asbat narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from Atiyyah, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: When the Trumpet is blown, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How can I enjoy when the keeper of the Trumpet has taken the Trumpet? And he bowed his forehead, listening when he would be commanded. His companions said: What shall we say? He said: Say: Allah suffices us, and He is the best Disposer."
"12706","12672 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Salamah ibn Sabur narrated to us, from Atiyyah, from Ibn Abbas, And do not bestow favor expecting more, who said: Do not give a man a gift hoping he will give you more than it."
"12707","12673 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Salih ibn Malik al-Khwarizmi narrated to us, Sawwar ibn Musab narrated to us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the earnings of slave women. I said to Ibn Abbas: Why did he forbid it? He said: Fearing they would fail and thus be failed."
"12708","12674 - Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Massisi narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Mubashshir ibn Ubayd, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bow four rakahs before Friday prayer and four after it without separating between them."
"12709","12675 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Tariq al-Wabishi narrated to us, Amr ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said at his departure to Badr: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has promised me Badr and to grant me their army as spoils; whoever kills a slain one shall have such-and-such of their spoils, if Allah wills, and whoever captures a captive shall have such-and-such of their spoils, if Allah wills. When they met, Allah cast terror into the hearts of the polytheists; when they fought, Allah routed them, and the swift of the people followed them, killing seventy and capturing seventy."
"12710","12676 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Isa al-Ramli narrated to us, from Ubaydah, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: He has not fasted who fasts perpetually."
"12711","12677 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Musarrif ibn Amr al-Yami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Husayn, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Abbas who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I have come to you from people for whom no shepherd provisions himself and no stallion neighs for them. So he ascended the pulpit, praised Allah, then said: O Allah, give us a rescuing, fertile, abundant, enveloping, immediate rain, not delayed. Then he descended, and none came to us from any direction but said: We have been revived."
"12712","12678 - Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Makkah is the inviolable sanctuary of Allah; its herbage shall not be uprooted, its trees shall not be cut, and its game shall not be frightened. al-Abbas said: O Messenger of Allah, except idhkhir, for it is for our smiths and the backs of our houses. He said: Except idhkhir."
"12713","12679 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Ata ibn Muslim al-Halabi narrated to us, al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Abu Bakara a young she-camel as gift, and he deemed it small. Then he said to me: Take it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), O my son, and say: We are working people; if you have an older one, send it to us. So I brought it, and he said: Cousin, direct it to the camels of charity. Then I came to him in the mosque and prayed Isha with him, and he said: Do you wish to spend the night with your aunt tonight? Evening has come. So I coincided with her night with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I came to her, she gave me supper and spread for me a cloak folded in four, and I lay on it. I said: I shall surely learn what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) does tonight. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and said: O Maymunah. She said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Has your nephew come to you? She said: Yes, here he is. He said: Did you not give him supper if you had anything? She said: I did. He said: And did you spread for him? She said: Yes. So he leaned to his bed but did not lie on it; he lay beside it and placed his head on the bed, and remained a while. I heard him snore in sleep, so I said: He has slept and will not wake, and will not stand tonight. Then he rose when, as I reckoned, a quarter or a third of the night had gone. He took his tooth-stick and ablution water and used the stick until I heard the grating of his teeth under it, while reciting these verses: Indeed in the creation of the heavens and the earth. Then he put down the stick, then stood to a waterskin, untied its thong. I wished to rise and pour for him, but I feared he might leave something of his practice. When he performed ablution he entered his prayer place and prayed four rakahs, reciting in each rakah about fifty verses, lengthening bowing and prostration in them. Then he came to his resting place and lay down a while and snored while asleep. I said: He will not stand tonight until morning. When two-thirds or half of the night or about that had gone, he rose and did the like; he entered his prayer place and prayed four rakahs about as long. Then he came to his bed and reclined on it and snored. I said: Sleep has overcome him; he will not stand until morning. Then he rose when a sixth of the night or less remained; he used the tooth-stick, then performed ablution, then entered his prayer place and magnified Allah, opening with the Opening of the Book, then reciting: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High. Then he bowed and prostrated, then stood and recited the Opening of the Book, then recited: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High. Then he bowed and prostrated, then stood and recited the Opening of the Book and: Say: O disbelievers. Then he bowed and prostrated, then stood with the Opening of the Book and: Say: O disbelievers. Then he bowed and prostrated, then stood and recited the Opening of the Book and: Say: He is Allah, One. Then he supplicated, bowed and prostrated. When he finished he sat until dawn broke, then called me. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Rise, for by Allah you were not asleep. So I rose, performed ablution, and prayed behind him. He recited the Opening of the Book and: Say: He is Allah, One. Then he bowed and prostrated, then stood in the second and recited the Opening of the Book and: Say: O disbelievers. When he gave salutation I heard him say: O Allah, place light in my heart, light in my hearing, light in my sight, light before me, light behind me, light on my right, light on my left, light above me, light beneath me, and magnify light for me, O Lord of the worlds."
"12714","12680 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us, Ata ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed over the dead, would say: O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, our present and our absent, our females and our males; whomsoever You keep alive among us, keep him alive upon Islam, and whomsoever You take among us, take him upon faith. O Allah, Your pardon, Your pardon."
"12715","12681 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Hammal narrated to us, Ata ibn Muslim al-Khaffaf narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Abbas who said: A slain man was killed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whose killer was unknown, so he ascended his pulpit and said: O people, is a slain man killed while I am among you and his killer unknown? If the people of heaven and earth gathered to kill a Muslim man, Allah would punish them without number or reckoning."
"12716","12682 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Awn ibn Sallam narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Abbas: And they forbid from him and keep away from him, revealed concerning Abu Talib; he used to forbid harming the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while keeping away from following him."
"12717","12683 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Dinar narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Said al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, my father has died; shall I free a slave on his behalf? He said: Yes."
"12718","12684 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid al-Raqqi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an army, and its banner was returned. Then he sent again, and it was returned with the misappropriation of a gazelle head of gold. So there was revealed: It is not for a prophet to misappropriate."
"12719","12685 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Rizqullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Nusayr al-Abiri narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Abbas who said: He only forbade solid silk."
"12720","12686 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Asid ibn Asim narrated to us, Amir ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Yaqub narrated to us, from Anbasah, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Abbas who said: Allah has companions on the Day of Resurrection at the right of the Throne, and both Hands of Allah are right, upon pulpits of light, their faces of light; they are neither prophets, nor martyrs, nor the truthful. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are they? He said: Those who love one another for the majesty of Allah, Exalted."
"12721","12687 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Husayn, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari who said: We set out as pilgrims; when we alighted at Batn Nakhl we saw the crescent. Some of the people said: It is three nights old, and some said: It is two nights old. So we came to Ibn Abbas and said: We saw the crescent; some of the people said it is three nights old, and some of the people said it is two nights old. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) extended it for its sighting, so it is the night you saw it."
"12722","12688 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, Amr ibn Murrah informed me, from Abu al-Bakhtari who said: I asked Ibn Abbas about advance payment for palms, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling palms until some is eaten of them and until it is secured. I said: What is secured? A man among the people said: Until it is harvested or secured."
"12723","12689 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us, al-Muharibi narrated to us, that he heard al-Amash mention, from Tarif ibn Maymun, from Ibn Abbas, raising it, who said: There is no man put in charge of ten but he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand chained to his neck until judgment is passed between him and them."
"12724","12690 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray eight rakahs at night and pray witr with three."
"12725","12691 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Umar ibn al-Subh, from Muqatil ibn Hayyan, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever hears the sound of a bell, or enters a church, synagogue, fire temple or idols, then says: There is no god but Allah, and we worship none but Allah, Allah writes for him reward equal to the number of those who did not say it, or he is written with Allah as a truthful one."
"12726","12692 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, they said: Hubayb ibn Habib, brother of Hamzah al-Zayyat, narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever establishes prayer, gives zakat, performs Hajj to the House, fasts Ramadan, and honors the guest, will enter Paradise."
"12727","12693 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhawi al-Qadi narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from al-Walid ibn al-Ayzar, from Ibn Abbas who said: Abu Jahl said: If Muhammad returns to pray behind the Maqam I shall surely assault him. It was said: There he is praying behind the Maqam. So he went toward him, then returned and said: By al-Lat and al-Uzza, there darkened between me and him battalions. Ibn Abbas said: Had he moved, the angels of punishment would have seized him. Then he recited: So let him call his council; We shall call the angels of punishment."
"12728","12694 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Juwayriyah al-Jarmi who said: I asked Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, about badhaq, and he said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preceded badhaq; whatever intoxicates is unlawful."
"12729","12695 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Juwayriyah al-Jarmi, from Ibn Abbas who said: Do you know concerning what this verse was revealed: O you who believe, do not ask about things which, if made plain to you, would harm you? Some people used to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in mockery; a man would say: Who is my father? And one would say: My camel is lost, where is my camel? So Allah revealed this verse."
"12730","12696 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya Abu al-Mualla al-Attar, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was one day praying, and a kid went to pass in front of him, so he hastened toward it. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying while a she-donkey of al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas was grazing that day in front of him."
"12731","12697 - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Massisi and Abu Zurah narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn Bilal narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadham, from al-Hakam, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr five rakahs, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness while sitting."
"12732","12698 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from his father, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took Usamah ibn Zayd behind him on the day of Arafah until he reached Muzdalifah, then took al-Fadl behind him until he reached the Aqabah pillar, and he kept chanting talbiyah until he stoned the Aqabah pillar."
"12733","12699 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us ahead on the night of Muzdalifah, the youngsters of Banu Abd al-Muttalib, upon donkeys; he kept patting our thighs and saying: My sons, do not stone the pillar until the sun rises."
"12734","12700 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas who said: I do not know whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Zuhr and Asr or not, but we recite."
"12735","12701 - Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Abu Shaybah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastened us by night from Muzdalifah to Mina, carrying us upon donkeys, and he kept striking our thighs, saying: My sons, do not stone the Aqabah pillar until the sun rises."
"12736","12702 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi and Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us ahead, the youngsters of Banu Abd al-Muttalib, upon donkeys, patting our thighs and saying: My sons, do not stone the Aqabah pillar until the sun rises."
"12737","12703 - Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan al-Massisi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas who said: I came, I and a boy of Banu Abd al-Muttalib, upon a donkey, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in prayer. So we let the donkey loose and entered the row, and two slave girls came racing, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated between them."
"12738","12704 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu al-Mualla al-Attar, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas, that what interrupts prayer was mentioned in his presence, and he said: What do you say about the kid? For the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying and a kid passed in front of him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastened toward the qiblah. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one day while a she-donkey of al-Fadl ibn Abbas was grazing in front of him."
"12739","12705 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas who said: When you have stoned the pillar, everything has become lawful for you except women. He said: As for me, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) scenting his head with musk; is that perfume or not?"
"12740","12706 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas who said: al-Sab ibn Jaththamah gifted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a portion of wild ass, and he returned it to him, saying: We are in ihram."
"12741","12707 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Musa ibn Mutayr narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: I witnessed Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to use the tooth-stick at night two or three times."
"12742","12708 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Jarjarai narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit al-Jazari narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Nafi, from Abd al-Ala al-Taymi, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Angel of Death came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the illness in which he was taken, and sought permission while his head was in the lap of Ali. He said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Go back, for we are occupied from you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know who this is, O Abu al-Hasan? This is the Angel of Death; enter rightly guided. When he entered he said: Your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, conveys salutation to you. He said: Where is Jibril? He said: He is not near me now; he is coming. So the Angel of Death went out until Jibril descended upon him. Jibril, peace be upon him, said to him while standing at the door: What brought you out, O Angel of Death? He said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought you. When they sat, Jibril said: Peace be upon you, O Abu al-Qasim; this is a farewell from me and from you. It reached me that the Angel of Death never greeted any household before him, nor will he greet after him."
"12743","12709 - Isa ibn al-Qasim al-Saydalani al-Baghdadi narrated to me, al-Hasan ibn Qazaah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever reviles my companions, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all people."
"12744","12710 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let every man eat of his sacrifice."
"12745","12711 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Safar, from Said ibn Shufi, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he left his house, would pray two rakahs, two rakahs, until he returned."
"12746","12712 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Yasin ibn Hammad al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Safar. And Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Said, that Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim wrote to him that Abu Ishaq narrated to him, from Said ibn Shufi al-Hamdani who said: I asked Ibn Abbas about prayer while travelling, and he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left his family travelling, he would pray two rakahs until he returned to his family."
"12747","12713 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bring out his family on the two Eids."
"12748","12714 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bring out his wives on the two Eids."
"12749","12715 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us. And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bring out his wives on the two Eids."
"12750","12716 - Ahmad ibn al-Khadir al-Khuzai al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdah al-Marwazi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari narrated to us, from Raqabah ibn Masqalah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis ibn Rabiah al-Nakhai who said: A man asked Ibn Abbas: Did you reach the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, I reached him while a boy, and his aim was to attend an Eid. So he went out, ordered a spear, and it was fixed for him near the house of Kathir ibn al-Salt. He admonished them, reminded them with verses of the Quran, and urged them to charity. I saw them reaching to their ears and throats to hand charity to Bilal. Then he returned to his family."
"12751","12717 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, from Wail ibn Dawud, from al-Bahiyy, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not give the kawdan anything, and gave it less than the share of the bachelors in strength and quality; and the kawdan is the slow mule."
"12752","12718 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us. And Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, they said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abu Khalid, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to open prayer with: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"12753","12719 - Ubayd ibn Kathir al-Tammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, Iyad ibn Said al-Thumali narrated to us, from Isa ibn Muslim al-Qurashi, from Amr ibn Abdullah ibn Hind al-Jamali, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Whoever shows enmity to a saint of Mine has declared war on Me. And I have never hesitated over anything I do as I hesitate over the death of the believer; he dislikes death and I dislike his distress. And perhaps My believing saint asks Me for wealth, and I turn him from wealth to poverty; had I turned him to wealth it would have been evil for him. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: By My might, majesty, exaltedness, splendor, beauty and elevation of station, no servant prefers My desire over his own desire but I fix his term before his sight, the heaven and earth guarantee his provision, and I am for him beyond the trade of every trader."
"12754","12720 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Qays al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Harun ibn Antarah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke his fast he would say: For You I fasted, and upon Your provision I broke my fast, so accept from me; indeed You are the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing."
"12755","12721 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Harun ibn Antarah, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left us no yellow or white except what is between its two covers. I stood to the hilt of his sword and found in its scabbard a sheet written therein: Whoever commits an offense, shelters an offender, ascribes himself to other than his father, or a freed slave to other than his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all people."
"12756","12722 - Abdullah ibn Zaydan al-Bajali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hammad ibn Amr al-Azdi narrated to us, Husayn al-Ashqar narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Masudi narrated to us, from Kathir al-Nawwa, from Maymun Abu Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the people of the mosque were expelled and Ali was left, people spoke about that, and it reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I did not expel you of my own accord, nor did I leave him; but Allah expelled you and left him. I am only a commanded servant; what I am commanded I do: I follow only what is revealed to me."
"12757","12723 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Hammad ibn Isa al-Absi narrated to us, from Ismail al-Suddi, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, raising it, who said: Allah created the Garden of Eden with His Hand, hung its fruits therein, and cleft its rivers therein. Then He looked into it and said: The believers have succeeded. He said: By My might, no miser shall dwell beside Me in you."
"12758","12724 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubadah ibn Ziyad al-Asadi narrated to us, Mudrik ibn Sulayman al-Tai narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophets banishment of al-Hakam ibn Abi al-As from Madinah to Taif was only because, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in his chamber, a man peeked at him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lizard, the lizard. He looked and it was al-Hakam. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go out; you shall not dwell with me in Madinah as long as I remain. So he banished him to Taif."
"12759","12725 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: He cursed women who visit graves, and those who take mosques and lamps over them."
"12760","12726 - Abdullah ibn Najiyah narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid al-Jarudi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is what leaves sufficiency, the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support."
"12761","12727 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qitrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jami al-Attar narrated, Dawud ibn Abd al-Hamid Abu Sulayman al-Kufi narrated, Abu al-Jarud narrated, from Habib ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating grapes by stripping them off the bunch."
"12762","12728 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih narrated, Abu Shihab narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in an open space of land with nothing before him."
"12763","12729 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Maymun narrated, al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated, from Layth, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The share of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), which Allah granted him, is a fifth of the fifth."
"12764","12730 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Awn ibn Sallam narrated, Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform the witr prayer with three rakahs."
"12765","12731 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated, from Yazid Abu Khalid - he is al-Dalani al-Wasiti - from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever visits a sick person and says: I ask Allah the Mighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to heal you, except that he recovers, unless his appointed term has come. Shubah said: He raised it to the Prophet once, and did not raise it twice."
"12766","12732 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever visits a sick person and says: I ask Allah the Mighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, except that he recovers, unless his appointed term has come."
"12767","12733 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the like of it."
"12768","12734 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, (H). And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated - both saying: Yahya ibn Adam narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abu Sinan, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a dead person after he had been buried."
"12769","12735 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Dawud al-Sukkari al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khulayd al-Hanafi narrated, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated, from al-Amash, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prophet among the prophets complained to his Lord, mighty and majestic, saying: O Lord, there is a servant of Yours who believes in You and acts in obedience to You, yet You withhold the world from him and lay trial open before him; and there is a servant of Yours who disbelieves in You and acts in disobedience to You, yet You withhold trial from him and lay the world open before him. So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed to him: Trial and servants belong to Me, and there is nothing except that it glorifies Me, declares My oneness, and magnifies Me. As for My believing servant, he has sins, so I withhold the world from him and lay trial open before him until he comes to Me, and I recompense him with good deeds; and as for My disbelieving servant, he has good deeds, so I withhold trial from him and lay the world open before him until he comes to Me, and I recompense him for his evil deeds."
"12770","12736 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Imran al-Sulami, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Quraysh said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Call upon your Lord for us to make al-Safa gold for us; if it becomes gold for us in the morning, we will follow you. So he called upon his Lord, mighty and majestic, and Jibril (peace be upon him) came to him and said: Your Lord conveys peace to you and says to you: If you wish, al-Safa will become gold for them in the morning, but whoever disbelieves among them, I will punish him with a punishment with which I have not punished anyone in the worlds; and if you wish, I will open for them the door of repentance and mercy. He said: Rather, the door of repentance and mercy."
"12771","12737 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Yusuf al-Qadi both said: Umar ibn Marzuq narrated, Shubah reported, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, he said: I heard Aba al-Hakam al-Sulami narrating from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril said to me: The month has ended at twenty-nine."
"12772","12738 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Yusuf al-Qadi both said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shubah reported, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abi al-Hakam al-Sulami, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the nabidh of the earthen jar, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the earthen jar and the gourd. And Ibn Abbas said: Whoever holds unlawful what Allah and His Messenger made unlawful, let him hold nabidh unlawful - meaning the nabidh of the jar."
"12773","12739 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, Yahya ibn Adam narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abi Razin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When (Indeed, you and what you worship besides Allah are fuel for Hell; you will enter it) was sent down, Abd Allah ibn al-Zibara said: I will dispute against Muhammad for you. He said: O Muhammad, is it not in what Allah sent down to you: (Indeed, you and what you worship besides Allah are fuel for Hell; you will enter it)? He said: Yes. He said: These Christians worship Isa, and these Jews worship Uzayr, and these Banu Tamim worship the angels - so are these in the Fire? Then Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: (Indeed, those for whom good has preceded from Us, they will be kept far from it)."
"12774","12740 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi Hassan al-Anmati narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, Sufyan al-Thawri and Shayban narrated, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Abi Razin, from Abi Yahya, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Quraysh: O company of Quraysh, there is no good in anyone worshipped besides Allah. They said: Do you not claim that Isa was a prophet and was a righteous servant? If you are truthful, then he is like their gods. So Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: (And when the son of Mary is presented as an example, your people turn away from it in clamour) - they raise a clamour - (And indeed, he is a sign of the Hour) - the emergence of Isa before the Day of Resurrection."
"12775","12741 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bashir, from Ubayd Allah ibn al-Musawir, he said: Ibn Abbas said - while he was defending Ibn al-Zubayr: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not one who eats his fill while his neighbour is hungry."
"12776","12742 - Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from al-Amash, from Abi Dawud, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Allah did not send a prophet except that after him there was a halt of people with whom He will fill Hell."
"12777","12743 - Said ibn al-Mughirah al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from a man called al-Hasan, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about one who performed one of the rites of Hajj before another, or delayed it, out of ignorance, unintentionally, and he said: There is no harm upon him."
"12778","12744 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yazid ibn Mihran Abu Khalid al-Khabbaz narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from al-Ajlah, from al-Dhayyal ibn Harmalah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Some people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a camel of ours strayed into a walled garden. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to it and said: Come. So it came lowering its head until he bridled it, and he gave it to its owners. Abu Bakr said to him: O Messenger of Allah, it is as if he knew that you are a prophet. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one between its two lava tracts except that he knows that I am a prophet, except the disbelievers among the jinn and mankind."
"12779","12745 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated, Sawwar ibn Musab narrated, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Amr ibn Sufyan, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Sodom and the towns around it were not destroyed until they cleaned their teeth with tooth-sticks and chewed gum in gatherings."
"12780","12746 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated, from al-Amash, from Ziyad ibn Husayn, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a group shooting arrows and said: Shoot, O sons of Ismail, for your father was an archer."
"12781","12747 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated, Awf narrated, from Ziyad ibn Husayn, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the morning of al-Aqabah, while he was upon his mount: Bring me pebbles to pick up - so I picked up for him pebbles of the size flung between fingers. When I placed them in his hand, he said: Yes, with the like of these - three times - and beware of excess, for those before you were destroyed only by excess in religion."
"12782","12747/2 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Awf, from Ziyad ibn Husayn, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the like of it."
"12783","12748 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated, (H). And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, (H). And Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Said al-Asbahani narrated - all saying: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated, from Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from Qatadah, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray two rakahs before Fajr, then sleep until he snored and breathed heavily, while prostrating or sitting, then stand and pray. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you have slept. He said: Ablution is only obligatory upon one who sleeps lying down, for when he lies down, his joints relax."
"12784","12749 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Abi al-Aliyah, he said: The cousin of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me - meaning Ibn Abbas - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw, on the night I was taken on the night journey, Musa ibn Imran (peace be upon him), a dark, tall, curly-haired man, as if he were one of the men of Shanuah; and I saw Isa ibn Maryam, a man of medium stature inclining to redness and whiteness, lank-haired; and I saw Malik, the keeper of the Fire; and I saw al-Dajjal - among the signs which Allah, mighty and majestic, showed me."
"12785","12750 - Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated, (H). And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated - both of them - from Qatadah, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate in distress: There is no god but Allah, the Mighty, the Wise; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the noble Throne; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the Mighty Throne."
"12786","12751 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the like of it."
"12787","12752 - Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi and Abu Zura both said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn Bilal narrated, Said ibn Bashir narrated, from Qatadah, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for the weakness of the weak and the sickness of the sick, I would have delayed the last Isha prayer."
"12788","12753 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shubah narrated, from Qatadah, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting for a servant to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta."
"12789","12754 - Abu Hanifah Muhammad ibn Hanifah al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad al-Habhabi narrated, Said ibn Suwayd al-Maghuli narrated, Imran al-Qattan narrated, from Qatadah, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The worst of food is the food of the wedding feast to which the satiated are invited and from which the hungry are kept away."
"12790","12755 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated, Ulailah ibn Badr narrated, Sayyar ibn Salamah narrated, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: He used to teach us the bowing as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach them; then he would steady himself for us in bowing, such that if a drop of water were dripped between his shoulders, it would neither move forward nor backward."
"12791","12756 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Rufay Abi al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon the valley of Ibn al-Azraq and said: What is this valley? They said: The valley of Ibn al-Azraq. He said: It is as if I see Musa (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descending, with his fervent crying out to his Lord in talbiyah. Then he came upon a mountain pass and said: What is this pass? It was said: Such-and-such pass. He said: It is as if I see Yunus ibn Matta upon a red curly-haired she-camel, its bridle of palm fibre, wearing a woollen cloak, while he recites the talbiyah. Abu al-Qasim said: Hammad ibn Salamah said: Ibn al-Azraq - though it is only al-Azraq."
"12792","12757 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated, Bishr ibn Umar al-Zahrani narrated, Aban ibn Yazid narrated, from Qatadah, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas: that a man cursed the wind, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse it, for it is commanded; and whoever curses a thing that does not deserve it, the curse falls back upon him."
"12793","12758 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated, from Qatadah, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), regarding His saying: (And We made him a guidance for the Children of Israel), he said: Musa was made a guidance for the Children of Israel; and regarding His saying: (So be not in doubt about meeting him), he said: About the meeting of Musa with his Lord, mighty and majestic."
"12794","12759 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi both said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from al-Jad Abi Uthman, from Abi Raja, from Ibn Abbas - narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever sees from his commander something he disapproves of, let him be patient, for there is no one who separates from the community and dies except that he dies the death of ignorance."
"12795","12760 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi narrated, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated, al-Jad Abu Uthman narrated, from Abi Raja, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Your Lord is Merciful. Whoever intends a good deed and does not do it, tenfold up to seven hundredfold up to many multiples is written for him; and whoever intends an evil deed and does not do it, a good deed is written for him, and if he does it, one evil deed is written against him, or He effaces it; and none perishes at the hands of Allah except one doomed to perish."
"12796","12761 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan, from Abi Raja, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the like of it."
"12797","12762 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated, Abd al-Hakim ibn Dhakwan narrated, from Abi Raja, from Ibn Abbas: that he said on a rainy day: The prayer is in the dwellings. Then he said: Do you find it strange? One better than us did it - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12798","12763 - Muhammad ibn Yaqub ibn Sawrah al-Baghdadi and Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Bukayr al-Tayalisi both narrated: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Salm ibn Zurayr narrated, he said: I heard Aba Raja, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ibn Said: I have hidden something for you - what is it? He said: Smoke. He said: Be gone."
"12799","12764 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti and Ali ibn Said al-Razi both said: Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated, he said: I heard Aba Raja al-Utaridi saying: I heard Ibn Abbas narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The affair of this ummah will remain close-knit until they speak about children and pre-decree."
"12800","12765 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah informed me, he said: I heard Aba Raja, Ibn Abbas narrated, he said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its people were the poor and needy, and I looked at the Fire and saw that most of its people were women."
"12801","12766 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani both said: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated, Abu al-Ashhab narrated, Abu Raja narrated, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its people were the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its people were women."
"12802","12767 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated, from Ayyub, from Abi Raja, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its people were the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its people were women."
"12803","12768 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated, Ayyub narrated, from Abi Raja, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its people were the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its people were women."
"12804","12769 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated, from Ayyub and Matar al-Warraq, from Abi Raja, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its people were the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its people were women."
"12805","12770 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir al-Muharibi narrated, Yahya ibn Yala ibn al-Harith narrated, from his father, from Bakr ibn Wail, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Abi Raja, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah."
"12806","12771 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated, Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Abi Raja, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date."
"12807","12772 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated, Awf narrated, from Said ibn Abi al-Hasan, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas when a man came to him and said: I am a man whose livelihood is only from the work of my hand, and I make these images. Ibn Abbas said: I find for you nothing except what I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say - I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever makes an image, Allah will punish him on the Day of Resurrection until he breathes a soul into it, and he will never breathe into it. He said: The man gasped a severe gasp and his face turned yellow. Then he said: Woe to you, if you refuse but to make, then take to this tree and everything in which there is no soul."
"12808","12773 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Awf, from Said ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the like of it."
"12809","12774 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Surayj ibn al-Numan al-Jawhari narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, Asim al-Ahwal narrated, from Abi Uthman, from Ibn Abbas: that al-Zubayr carried a horse in the path of Allah, then found a horse from its offspring being sold, and he was forbidden from buying it."
"12810","12775 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Yasin ibn Hammad al-Makhzumi narrated, (H). And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated - both saying: Abu Aqil al-Dawraqi narrated, from Abi Nadrah, from Ibn Abbas, regarding the saying of Allah, mighty and majestic: (Those who stay behind among the believers, other than those with hurt, are not equal), he said: They were a people in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who did not go out to battle with him because of illnesses, sicknesses, and pains, while others, healthy, did not go out to battle with him; and the sick were excused above the healthy."
"12811","12776 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, (H). And Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us - both saying: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Shaddad ibn Said al-Rasibi narrated, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abi Nadrah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of the youth of Quraysh, do not commit adultery; whoever guards his private part, Paradise is his."
"12812","12777 - Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abi Nadrah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first for whom the earth will split open, and it is no boast."
"12813","12778 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah and Ali ibn Bahr both narrated: Ghassan ibn Mudar narrated, from Said ibn Yazid, from Abi Nadrah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Whoever wishes to hold unlawful what Allah and His Messenger made unlawful, let him hold the nabidh of the jar unlawful."
"12814","12779 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, (H). And Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated - both saying: al-Bara ibn Abd Allah al-Ghanawi narrated, he said: I heard Aba Nadrah saying: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge at the end of his prayer from four things, saying: I seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the grave; I seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the Fire; I seek refuge in Allah from trials, what is apparent of them and what is hidden; I seek refuge in Allah from the trial of the one-eyed liar."
"12815","12780 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated, Abu Maslamah narrated, from Abi Nadrah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I visited my maternal aunt and it coincided with the night of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in a long pre-dawn prayer, performed ablution thoroughly, then stood praying. I stood, performed ablution, and came to his side; when he knew I wanted to pray, he took my hand and placed me at his right. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and performed witr with seven or nine, then bowed two rakahs, then laid his side down until I heard his breathing, then the prayer was established and he went out to the prayer."
"12816","12781 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated, Sallam al-Tawil narrated, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Abi Nadrah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he bowed, levelled himself, such that if water were poured upon his back it would settle."
"12817","12782 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated, Awf narrated, (H). And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Haytham al-Muadhdhin narrated, from Awf, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken on the night journey, he woke in Makkah and sat apart, grieved. The enemy of Allah, Abu Jahl, passed by him and said as if mocking: Was there anything? He said: Yes. He said: I was taken by night to Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: Then you woke up among us? He said: Yes. He did not show him that he disbelieved him, fearing that if he called his people to him, they would deny him the report. He said: What if I call your people to you - will you narrate to them what you narrated to me? He said: Yes. So Abu Jahl said: O Banu Kab ibn Luayy, come forth. The gatherings broke up until they sat with the two of them. Abu Jahl said: Narrate to your people what you narrated to me. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was taken by night. He said: To where? He said: To Bayt al-Maqdis. They said: Then you woke up among us? He said: Yes. Some clapped, and some placed his hand upon his head, astonished at the lie, as he claimed; and among the people were those who had travelled to that mosque and seen it. They said: Can you describe the mosque for us? He said: Yes. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So I described it for them until some of the description became confused for me. He said: So the mosque was brought while I was looking at it, until it was placed before the house of Aqil or the house of Iqal, and I described it while looking at it. The people said: As for the description, by Allah, he has got it right."
"12818","12783 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Suwayd al-Dhari narrated, Salih al-Murri narrated, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which speech is most beloved to Allah? He said: The one who alights and departs. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the one who alights and departs? He said: The companion of the Quran who strikes at its beginning until he reaches its end, and at its end until he reaches its beginning."
"12819","12784 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Shabab al-Usfuri narrated, Amr ibn Asim narrated, Salih al-Murri narrated, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, does medicine avail against pre-decree? He said: Medicine is part of pre-decree, and it may benefit by the permission of Allah."
"12820","12785 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated, (H). And Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated - both saying: Hammam narrated, from Qatadah, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate meat off a shoulder, then prayed and did not perform ablution."
"12821","12786 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated, Said ibn Sufyan al-Jahdari narrated, al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated, from Uqbah ibn Abi Thubayt al-Rasibi, from Abi al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Remember Allah with a remembrance such that the hypocrites say: You are showing off."
"12822","12787 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Abu Hilal al-Rasibi narrated, Uqbah ibn Abi Thubayt al-Rasibi narrated, from Abi al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise are those whose ears are filled with the good praise of people while they hear; and the people of the Fire are those whose ears are filled with the evil praise of people while they hear."
"12823","12788 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Taymi narrated, Salih ibn Abd Allah Abu Yahya narrated, from Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri, from Abi al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took hold of the two doorposts, while we were in the house, and said: O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, is there anyone among you from other than you? They said: A nephew of ours. He said: The nephew of a people is of them. Then he said: O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, when distress, fever, hardship, or adversity befalls you, say: Allah, Allah, our Lord, He has no partner."
"12824","12789 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Dubai narrated, Amr ibn Malik narrated, from Abi al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: (For him are successive angels before him and behind him) - he said: It is for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12825","12790 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Yahya ibn Amr ibn Malik narrated, from his father, from Abi al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: (On the Day We fold the heaven like the folding of a scroll for writings) - he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a scribe called al-Sijill."
"12826","12791 - Muhammad ibn al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Bishr ibn Hujr al-Sami narrated, (H). And Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Affan narrated - both saying: Nuh ibn Qays narrated, from Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri, from Abi al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, he said: There was a beautiful woman who used to pray behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); some people would go forward, and some would lag behind to look at her. So Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: (And We know those who go forward among you, and We know those who lag behind)."
"12827","12792 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, Jafar ibn Jasr ibn Farqad narrated, my father narrated, from Amr ibn Malik, from Abi al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Greatest Name of Allah, by which if He is called upon He answers, is in this verse of Al Imran: (Say: O Allah, Owner of sovereignty, You give sovereignty to whom You will) to its end."
"12828","12793 - Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid al-Jarudi narrated, from his father, Malik ibn Yahya ibn Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri narrated, from his father, from his grandfather Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri, from Abi al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever swears an oath and sees something better than it, let him do it, for that is its expiation - except in divorce or manumission."
"12829","12794 - Abu Shuayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated, Yahya ibn Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri narrated, from his father, from Abi al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you did not sin, Allah would bring a people who sin and He would forgive them."
"12830","12795 - Abu Shuayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated, Yahya ibn Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri narrated, from his father, from Abi al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The expiation of sin is remorse."
"12831","12796 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, (H). And Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated - both saying: Yahya ibn Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri narrated, from his father, from Abi al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer, he would say: There is no god but Allah alone, He has no partner; to Him belongs sovereignty, and to Him belongs praise; He gives life and causes death, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate does not avail him against You."
"12832","12797 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salm al-Umayri narrated, Malik ibn Yahya ibn Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri narrated, from his father, from his grandfather Amr ibn Malik, from Abi al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah said: I created good and evil, so glad tidings to one at whose hands I decreed good, and woe to one at whose hands I decreed evil."
"12833","12798 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salm al-Umayri narrated, Malik ibn Yahya narrated, from his father, from his grandfather Amr ibn Malik, from Abi al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I have not seen anything better sought, nor quicker to be attained, than a fresh good deed for an old sin: (Indeed, good deeds remove evil deeds; that is a reminder for those who remember)."
"12834","12799 - Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated, Malik ibn Yahya ibn Amr ibn Malik narrated, from his father, from Amr ibn Malik, from Abi al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas - raising the hadith - that he said: Whoever says: Glory be to Allah and with His praise; I seek the forgiveness of Allah and turn to Him in repentance, except that it is written as he said it, then hung upon the Throne, and no sin its doer commits effaces it until he meets Allah, while it is sealed as he said it."
"12835","12800 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Muammal ibn Ismail narrated, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Amr ibn Malik, from Abi al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both - and we know it only as raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Islam is built upon five: testimony that there is no god but Allah, prayer, and the fast of Ramadan; so whoever abandons one of them is a disbeliever whose blood is lawful."
"12836","12801 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah both said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib narrated to me, Yahya ibn Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri narrated, from his father, from Abi al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, he said: One of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pitched his tent over a grave, not thinking it was a grave, when behold, a man was reciting: (Blessed is He in whose hand is sovereignty) until he completed it. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I pitched my tent over a grave, not thinking it was a grave, when behold, a man was reciting Tabarak until he completed it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is the preventer, it is the saviour; it saves him from the punishment of the grave."
"12837","12802 - Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated, Rawh ibn al-Musayyab narrated, from Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri, from Abi al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas: (And when you mention your Lord alone in the Quran, they turn their backs in aversion) - he said: The devils."
"12838","12803 - Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Abdawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: In Hell there is a valley from which Hell itself seeks refuge four hundred times every day; that valley is prepared for the show-offs among the ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): for the bearer of the Book of Allah, for the one who gives charity for other than the sake of Allah, for the pilgrims to the House of Allah, and for the one who goes out in the path of Allah."
"12839","12804 - Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Abdawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A servant who obeys Allah and obeys his masters - Allah will admit him into Paradise seventy autumns before his masters. The master will say: O Lord, this was my servant in the world. He will say: I recompensed him for his deed, and I recompensed you for your deed."
"12840","12805 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq reported, Mamar reported, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abi al-Shatha, that Ibn Abbas informed him, he said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eight together and seven together."
"12841","12806 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eight together and seven together."
"12842","12807 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed eight rakahs together and seven rakahs together, without illness or excuse."
"12843","12808 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in Madinah seven and eight: Zuhr and Asr, and Maghrib and Isha."
"12844","12809 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever cannot find a waist-wrapper, let him wear trousers; and whoever cannot find sandals, let him wear leather socks."
"12845","12810 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Trousers are for one who cannot find a waist-wrapper, and leather socks are for one who cannot find sandals - meaning the one in ihram."
"12846","12811 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Salih ibn Hatim ibn Wardan narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated, Ayyub narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one in ihram, when he cannot find a waist-wrapper, let him wear trousers; and when he cannot find sandals, let him wear leather socks."
"12847","12812 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Uthman narrated, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abi al-Shatha Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed them and said: When the one in ihram cannot find a waist-wrapper, let him wear trousers; and when he cannot find sandals, then leather socks."
"12848","12813 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim narrated, Said ibn Zayd narrated, Amr ibn Dinar narrated, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed the people at Arafah and said: Whoever cannot find sandals, let him wear leather socks; and whoever cannot find a waist-wrapper, let him wear trousers."
"12849","12814 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, (H). And Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated, (H). And Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, Abu Zafar Abd al-Salam ibn Mutahhar narrated - all saying: Shubah narrated, Amr ibn Dinar informed me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Zayd saying: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering the sermon at Arafat, saying: Whoever cannot find sandals, let him wear leather socks; and whoever cannot find a waist-wrapper, let him wear trousers."
"12850","12815 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar: that Aba al-Shatha Jabir ibn Zayd informed him that Ibn Abbas informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever cannot find a waist-wrapper and finds trousers, let him wear them; and whoever cannot find sandals and finds leather socks, let him wear them."
"12851","12816 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Yala ibn Muslim, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between al-Zubayr and Ibn Masud."
"12852","12817 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Yala ibn Muslim, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas: (And do not say of anything: I will do that tomorrow, except with the will of Allah; and remember your Lord when you forget) - that you say: If Allah wills."
"12853","12818 - Ahmad ibn Shuayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasai narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Mansur informed me, Mubashshir ibn Abd Allah narrated, Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated, from Yala ibn Muslim, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were emigrants because they abandoned the polytheists; and among the Ansar there were emigrants because Madinah was a dwelling to come to - so they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of al-Aqabah."
"12854","12819 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Jubarah ibn Mughallis narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever forgets to send blessings upon me misses the path to Paradise."
"12855","12820 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated, Umar ibn Ubayd narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the meat of donkeys, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that horse meat be eaten."
"12856","12821 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, Hammam narrated, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was proposed the daughter of Hamzah, and he said: She is not lawful for me; she is the daughter of my brother through suckling, and what is unlawful through lineage is unlawful through suckling."
"12857","12822 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was proposed the daughter of Hamzah, and he said: She is the daughter of my brother through suckling, and what is unlawful through lineage is unlawful through suckling."
"12858","12823 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Will you not marry the daughter of Hamzah? He said: She is the daughter of my brother through suckling."
"12859","12824 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas - Shubah raised it - he said: The black dog and the menstruating woman interrupt the prayer."
"12860","12825 - Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated, Said ibn Bashir narrated, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined the two prayers in the expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq."
"12861","12826 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It is of the Sunnah to combine the two prayers while travelling."
"12862","12827 - al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya and al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Bistam al-Zafarani both said: Yusuf ibn Hammad al-Mani narrated, Abd al-Ala narrated, from Said, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Immoral women are those who marry themselves off without evidence."
"12863","12828 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Amr ibn Abd Allah al-Awdi narrated, Waki narrated, from Said ibn Bashir, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Circumcision is a Sunnah for men and an honour for women."
"12864","12829 - al-Sari ibn Sahl al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Rashid narrated, Mujjaah ibn al-Zubayr narrated, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The martyr will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and set up for reckoning, and the charitable one will be brought and set up for reckoning; then the people of trial will be brought, and neither scale will be set up for them nor register unrolled for them, and reward will be poured upon them in abundance, until the people of well-being in the standing place will wish that their bodies had been cut with scissors, because of the excellence of Allah's reward for them."
"12865","12830 - Ahmad Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated, Amr ibn Yahya ibn Abi Habib narrated, Habib ibn Abi Habib narrated, from Amr ibn Harim, he said: Jabir ibn Zayd was asked about prayer and its times, and he said: Ibn Abbas said: The Fajr prayer is between the rising of dawn and the rising of the sun's rays, and its time departs; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once travelled by night, then halted for rest at the end of the night, and did not wake until the sun rose or part of it, and he did not pray until it had risen, and he prayed; and it is the middle prayer."
"12866","12831 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated, Sufyan ibn Habib narrated, from Shubah, from Abi al-Anbas, from Abi al-Shatha, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set the ransom of the people of Badr at four hundred."
"12867","12832 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi narrated, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from al-Ghitrif, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Trustworthy Spirit, he said: The Lord, mighty and majestic, said: The good deeds and evil deeds of the servant will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and some will cancel out others; if one good deed remains, Allah will admit him into Paradise. He said: I said: What if no good deed remains? He said: (Those are they from whom We accept the best of what they did, and overlook their evil deeds, among the companions of Paradise). He said: I said: What about His saying: (No soul knows what is hidden for them of comfort for the eyes)? He said: It is the servant who does a secret deed, which Allah keeps secret for him on the Day of Resurrection, and he sees comfort for the eyes."
"12868","12833 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi and Muhammad ibn Kaysan both said: Abu Hudhayfah narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Duwayd, from Ismail ibn Thawban, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The evil eye is real, the evil eye is real; it brings down the one on the mountain peak."
"12869","12834 - Abu Zakariyya al-Dinawari al-Basri narrated to us, Said ibn Muhammad ibn Thawab al-Husri narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah al-Qurashi narrated, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best doors of righteousness are charity."
"12870","12835 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar: that Ibn Abbas recited this verse: (Today I have perfected for you your religion and completed upon you My favour) to the end of the verse, while a Jew was with him. He said: Had this verse been sent down upon us, we would have taken its day as a festival. Ibn Abbas said: It was sent down on the day of two festivals: Friday and the day of Arafah."
"12871","12836 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, (H). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Abu Muslim al-Kashshi both narrated: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I was with my father at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) there was a man confiding with him, and he was as if turning away from my father. We left him, and he said to me: Did you not see your cousin as if turning away from me? I said to him: O father, there was a man with him confiding with him. He said: Was there anyone with him? I said: Yes. We returned, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, I said to Abd Allah such-and-such, and he said to me such-and-such, and was there anyone with you? He said: Yes, and did you see him, O Abd Allah? I said: Yes. He said: That was Jibril; he is the one who kept me from you."
"12872","12837 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim both said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, (H). And Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated - both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in what the sleeper sees, one day at midday, dishevelled and dusty, with a flask of blood in his hand. I said: May my father and mother be ransomed for you, O Messenger of Allah, what is this? He said: This is the blood of al-Husayn and his companions; I have not ceased gathering it since today. It was counted, and he was found to have been killed that day."
"12873","12838 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Jarir narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas - as Abu Salamah reckons - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, and her father wished to marry her to him. She prepared food and drink, invited her father and some people of Quraysh, and they ate and drank. Khadijah said to her father: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah proposes to me; stand and marry her to him. She perfumed him with khaluq and dressed him in a robe, as they used to do with fathers when they married off their daughters. When the intoxication wore off him, he looked, and behold, he was perfumed and wearing a robe. He said: What is the matter with me? She said: You married me to Muhammad. He said: I married you to the orphan of Abu Talib? No, by my life. Khadijah said: Are you not ashamed? Do you wish to disgrace yourself, informing Quraysh and the people that you were drunk? She kept at him until he agreed."
"12874","12839 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas - as Hammad reckons - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Khadijah: I hear a voice and see a light, and I fear there may be madness in me. Khadijah said: Allah would not do that to you, O son of Abd Allah. Then she came to Waraqah ibn Nawfal and mentioned that to him. He said: If he is truthful, then this is a namus like the namus of Musa; and if he is sent and I am alive, I will strengthen him, support him, and aid him."
"12875","12840 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas - as I reckon, Hammad doubted - he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in Makkah fifteen years: seven or eight seeing the light and hearing the voice, and eight receiving revelation; and he stayed in Madinah ten."
"12876","12841 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver the sermon leaning against a trunk before taking the pulpit; when he took the pulpit and moved to it, the trunk moaned, so he embraced it and it calmed. He said: Had I not embraced it, it would have moaned until the Day of Resurrection."
"12877","12842 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, freedman of Banu Hashim, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: How old was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day he died? He said: I did not think one like you among his people would be unaware of that. He said: I said: I asked and was given differing answers, so I wished to know your saying on it. He said: Will you count? I said: Yes. He said: Take forty - he was sent with it; and fifteen his stay in Makkah, in safety and fear; and ten his emigration in Madinah."
"12878","12843 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated, from Yunus, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died at the age of sixty-five; and al-Hasan used to say: He died at the age of sixty."
"12879","12844 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died at the age of sixty-five."
"12880","12845 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated, Hushaym narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away at the age of sixty-five."
"12881","12846 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated, Awf narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave the cupper his wage; had it been unlawful, he would not have given him."
"12882","12847 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated, Abu Hilal narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and paid him his hire; had it been impure, he would not have hired him."
"12883","12848 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Hammad al-Shuaythi narrated, Ibn Awf narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and paid him; had he known it impure, he would not have given him."
"12884","12849 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq reported, Mamar reported, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave the cupper his wage; had it been ill-gotten, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not have given him."
"12885","12850 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, (H). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated - both saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and paid him; had it been impure, he would not have given him."
"12886","12851 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu al-Shatha Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated, Waki narrated, from Zayd ibn Ibrahim, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped, and he would never wrong a hireling of his hire."
"12887","12852 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: I was informed that Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and paid him; had he known any harm in it, he would not have given him."
"12888","12853 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and paid the cupper his wage; had it been unlawful, he would not have given him."
"12889","12854 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Abd Allah ibn al-Ajlah narrated, from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and paid him; had it been unlawful, he would not have given him."
"12890","12854/2 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sahl narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Tammam narrated, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave the cupper his wage; had it been impure, he would not have given him."
"12891","12855 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Hammad al-Shuaythi narrated, Ibn Awn narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to shorten the prayer between Madinah and Makkah, fearing none but Allah."
"12892","12856 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman, brother of Abu Hurrah, narrated, Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to shorten the prayer between Makkah and Madinah, fearing none but Allah."
"12893","12857 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Qurrah ibn Khalid and Said ibn Abd al-Rahman both narrated: Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) travelled from Makkah to Madinah and prayed two rakahs, fearing none but Allah."
"12894","12858 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, (H). And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Maslamah ibn Qanab narrated, Abu Hilal narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) travelled between Makkah and Madinah, fearing none but Allah - or he said: fearing only Allah - and prayed two rakahs."
"12895","12859 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq reported, Mamar reported, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would travel from Madinah to Makkah, fearing none but Allah, and pray two rakahs, two rakahs."
"12896","12860 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas: the like of it."
"12897","12861 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rakahs between Makkah and Madinah, fearing none but Allah."
"12898","12863 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated, (H). And Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated, (H). And Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar reported - all saying: Hushaym narrated, Mansur ibn Zadham narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out from Madinah to Makkah, fearing none but Allah, and prayed two rakahs until he departed."
"12899","12864 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rakahs between Makkah and Madinah, fearing none but Allah."
"12900","12865 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, (H). And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Yusuf al-Qadi both said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated - both saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) picked meat off a shoulder, then stood and prayed, and did not perform ablution."
"12901","12866 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid narrated to us, my father narrated, Muhammad ibn Maslamah narrated, (H). And Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid reported, (H). And Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Abd al-Ala narrated - all of them - from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) picked meat off a bone, then prayed and did not touch water."
"12902","12867 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, al-Muharibi narrated, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) picked meat off a shoulder, then stood and prayed, and did not perform ablution."
"12903","12868 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Awn ibn al-Hakam ibn Sinan al-Bahili narrated, Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I was among those sent ahead with the baggage of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Muzdalifah to Mina."
"12904","12869 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Ubayd Allah al-Qurashi al-Faqih narrated, Muhammad ibn Amr Abu Sahl al-Ansari narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed for the people of Madinah Dhu al-Hulayfah, for the people of Sham al-Juhfah, for the people of Yemen Yalamlam, and for the people of Najd Qarn."
"12905","12870 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ismail ibn Abd Allah, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Revelation descended upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was forty years old; he stayed in Makkah thirteen years, in Madinah ten, and died at the age of sixty-three."
"12906","12871 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Hurayth al-Marwazi narrated, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated, Ibn Awn narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) extended his hand toward Hudhayfah, but Hudhayfah held back until he went and performed ghusl, then he came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I was in a state of major ritual impurity. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslim does not become impure."
"12907","12872 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Hurayth narrated, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated, Ibn Awn narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded a caller, who called out on a rainy day: Pray in your dwellings."
"12908","12873 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: A funeral passed by Ibn Abbas and al-Hasan ibn Ali (may Allah be pleased with them); al-Hasan stood up while Ibn Abbas remained seated. Al-Hasan said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once stood for the funeral of a Jew or a Jewess that passed by him? Ibn Abbas said: Yes indeed — and he sat."
"12909","12874 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin: that a funeral passed by Ibn Abbas and al-Hasan ibn Ali, so one of them stood and the other sat. The one who stood said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood? The other said: Yes — and he sat down."
"12910","12875 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin: that Ibn Abbas said concerning this verse: {And upon those who can bear it, a ransom of feeding a poor person} — then the other verse abrogated it: {So whoever of you witnesses the month, let him fast it}."
"12911","12876 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Wasil, the freedman of Abu Uyaynah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas: that Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) divorced his wife, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The divorce of Umm Ayyub was a sin. Ibn Sirin said: Al-hub means sin."
"12912","12877 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Misar narrated, from Simak al-Hanafi, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: When the beginning of al-Muzzammil was revealed, their standing in prayer was like their standing in Ramadan, or nearly like their standing in Ramadan, and between its beginning and its end there was a year."
"12913","12878 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Ikrimah ibn Ammar, from Abu Zumayl al-Hanafi, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a cloak of the finest Yemeni cloth."
"12914","12879 - Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated, from Simak Abu Zumayl al-Hanafi, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard him say: On the day of Hunayn the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) acquired spoils of war and distributed them among the people, so the Ansar said: We bear the fighting, while the spoils go to others. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he sent to them to gather together, then he came to them and said: O company of the Ansar, is there anyone among you from other than you? They said: No, except a nephew of ours and a freedman of ours. He said: The nephew of a people is of them, and the freedman of a people is of them. He said: O company of the Ansar, are you not pleased that the people should go away with sheep and cattle, while you go away with Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They said: We are indeed pleased."
"12915","12880 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, (H). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, (H). And Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated — all saying: Abd Rabbihi ibn Bariq al-Hanafi narrated, Simak al-Hanafi related to me, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of my nation has two forerunners die before him, Allah will admit him to Paradise. Aishah said: And whoever has one forerunner die before him? He said: And whoever has one forerunner die before him, O favored one. She said: And whoever has no forerunner? He said: Then I am the forerunner of my nation — they will never be afflicted with the like of me."
"12916","12881 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhuyi, the judge, narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari narrated, al-Nadr ibn Muhammad al-Jurashi narrated, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated, Abu Zumayl narrated, Ibn Abbas narrated, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed for rain, so the people were rained upon until a canal flowed for forty days, and in the morning the people were saying: Such-and-such a star has indeed told the truth, and among them were those who said: This is a mercy which Allah has bestowed."
"12917","12882 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jammal al-Isbahani narrated to us, Hamdan ibn Yusuf al-Sulami narrated, (H). And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhuyi, the judge, narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari narrated — both saying: Al-Nadr ibn Muhammad al-Jurashi narrated, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated, Abu Zumayl narrated, Ibn Abbas narrated, he said: The people were rained upon in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the morning some of the people are grateful and some of them are ungrateful. They said: This is a mercy which Allah has bestowed — while some of them said: Such-and-such a star has indeed told the truth. Then this verse was sent down: {Nay, I swear by the setting-places of the stars} up to: {And you make your provision that you deny}."
"12918","12883 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jammal narrated to us, Hamdan ibn Yusuf al-Sulami narrated, al-Nadr ibn Muhammad narrated, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated, Abu Zumayl al-Hanafi narrated, Ibn Abbas related to me, he said: The polytheists used to say: Here I am at Your service, You have no partner — so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: Woe to you, enough, enough! But they would say: Except a partner who belongs to You, whom You own and whatever he owns. They would say this while circumambulating the House."
"12919","12884 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jammal narrated to us, Hamdan ibn Yusuf al-Sulami narrated, al-Nadr ibn Muhammad al-Jurashi narrated, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated, Abu Zumayl related to me, Ibn Abbas related to me, he said: I saw upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the finest of Yemeni garments."
"12920","12885 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhuyi narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari narrated, al-Nadr ibn Muhammad al-Jurashi narrated, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated, Abu Zumayl narrated, Ibn Abbas related to me, he said: The people would not look at Abu Sufyan nor sit with him, so he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Three things I offer you. He said: Yes. He said: I have the most beautiful and comeliest of the Arabs, Umm Habibah, the daughter of Abu Sufyan — I will marry her to you. He said: Yes. He said: And Muawiyah — appoint him a scribe before you. He said: Yes. He said: And appoint me to fight the disbelievers as I used to fight the Muslims. He said: Yes."
"12921","12886 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Umar ibn Khalaf ibn Ishaq ibn Mirsal al-Khathami narrated, my uncle Ismail ibn Mirsal related to me, from Abu Zumayl al-Hanafi, Ibn Abbas related to me, he said: The Muslims would not look at Abu Sufyan nor speak openly with him, so he said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), three things I offer you: I have the most beautiful and comeliest of the Arabs, Umm Habibah — I will marry her to you. He said: Yes. He said: And appoint Muawiyah a scribe before you. He said: Yes. He said: And appoint me to fight the disbelievers as I used to fight the Muslims. He said: Yes."
"12922","12887 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated, Hushaym narrated, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Barakah ibn al-Walid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah curse the Jews — fats were forbidden to them, yet they sold them and consumed their price. And when Allah, mighty and majestic, forbids eating a thing, He forbids its price."
"12923","12888 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Makhlad al-Wasiti narrated, he said: I found in my father's book: Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated, from Matar al-Warraq, from Abu Yazid al-Madini, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among poetry there is wisdom, and among eloquence there is magic."
"12924","12889 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya narrated, Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated, from Abu Yazid al-Madini, from Ibn Abbas, he said: We used to recite this: {The heavens almost split apart from above them}."
"12925","12890 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Isbahani narrated to us, Rawh ibn Abd al-Mumin narrated, Salamah ibn Raja narrated, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Farrukh narrated, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to delay the night prayer until a third of the night had passed; that is why it was called al-atamah, because he would enter deep into the night with it."
"12926","12891 - Yusuf the judge narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, Shubah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Suhayb, a man of the people of Basra, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I passed, along with a boy of Quraysh, upon a donkey in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, yet he did not turn away; and two young girls of the Banu Abd al-Muttalib came and clung to his knees, so he separated them, yet he did not turn away. Thus Shubah narrated it from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Suhayb — while Mansur differed from him."
"12927","12892 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Abu al-Sahba, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I came forward upon a donkey, with a companion riding behind me from the Banu Abd al-Muttalib, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying in an open land. We dismounted, then came until we entered the prayer, leaving the donkey in front of them, and he paid no attention to that. Then two young girls of the Banu Abd al-Muttalib came running, one following the other, until they reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, so he separated them, and he paid no attention to that."
"12928","12893 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Isbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abu Rafi, from Ibn Abbas: that he said to Umar: You accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was pleased with you."
"12929","12894 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Shubah narrated, from Qatadah, from Musa ibn Salamah, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas, saying: I am in Mecca — how should I pray? He said: Two units — the practice of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12930","12895 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father related to me, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated, Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated, from Qatadah, from Musa ibn Salamah, he said: We were with Ibn Abbas in Mecca, so we said: When we are with you we pray four units, but when we return to our lodgings we pray two units. He said: That is the practice of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), even if it displeases you."
"12931","12896 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh and Talut ibn Abbad narrated — both saying: Suwayd ibn Hatim narrated, from Qatadah, from Musa ibn Salamah, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the prayer at al-Abtah, and he said: Two units — the practice of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12932","12897 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, Abu al-Tayyah narrated, from Musa ibn Salamah, he said: I set out with Sinan ibn Salamah with two sacrificial camels, and when we feared for them we became burdened by their affair. Sinan said: If only we reach the town, we could seek knowledge of this matter. When we arrived I said: Will you visit Ibn Abbas at the watering place to converse with him? So Sinan asked him about the matter of his two camels, and he said: You have come upon the well-informed one. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent so-and-so al-Aslami and sent along with him eighteen sacrificial camels, and he said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), what if one of them becomes exhausted under my care? He said: Slaughter it, then dip its sandal in its blood, then strike it upon its flank, and neither you nor anyone of your company or your companions may eat from it."
"12933","12898 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Musa ibn Salamah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the like of it."
"12934","12899 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abd al-Warith narrated, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Musa ibn Salamah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the like of it."
"12935","12900 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Isbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever makes an image in this world will be charged on the Day of Resurrection to breathe the soul into it, yet he will never breathe into it."
"12936","12901 - Yusuf the judge narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shubah informed us, (H). And Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, (H). And Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, (H). And Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated, (H). And Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, Shubah narrated, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed at Dhu al-Hulayfah, then called for a sacrificial camel and marked the right side of its hump, then wiped the blood from it and garlanded it with two sandals; then his mount was brought, and when he sat upon it and it stood upright with him at al-Bayda, he entered ihram."
"12937","12902 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Isa al-Tai narrated, Talhah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram after the noon prayer at al-Bayda."
"12938","12903 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Umar ibn Hafs al-Hawdi narrated, Hammam narrated, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan: that Ibn Abbas was asked about advance payment (salam), so he said: I bear witness that Allah has permitted it, and He sent down concerning it the longest verse in the Book of Allah: {O you who believe, when you contract a debt for a specified term, write it down}."
"12939","12904 - Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated, he said: I found in my father's book, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit the House every night of the nights of Mina."
"12940","12905 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Shubah, Qatadah related to me, from Abu Mijlaz, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the witr prayer, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A single unit at the end of the night."
"12941","12906 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Khallad al-Bahili narrated, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated, Shubah narrated, from Qatadah, from Abu Mijlaz, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about something of the matter of the pebbles, and he said: I do not know whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw six or seven."
"12942","12907 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Tasnimi narrated, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated, from Qatadah, he said: It has reached us that when this verse was revealed, the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah advances in the prohibition of wine — so they would drink it as long as prayer was not due, and when prayer came they would refrain from it, while intoxication from it was forbidden to them. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down its prohibition in Surat al-Maidah, so it is forbidden, its little and its much, what intoxicates of it and what does not intoxicate. {Nor in a state of major impurity except passing through} — so He permitted the traveler, when traveling and in major impurity and finding no water, to perform tayammum and pray."
"12943","12908 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Tasnimi narrated, Rawh narrated, Shubah narrated, from Qatadah, from Lahiq ibn Humayd, from Ibn Abbas — with this hadith."
"12944","12909 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us — both saying: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated, Hibban ibn Ubayd Allah Abu Zuhayr narrated, Abd Allah ibn Buraydah narrated, from his father. And Abu Mijlaz narrated, from Ibn Abbas: that the banner of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was black, and his standard was white."
"12945","12910 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us — both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Humayd, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani: that a Bedouin said to Ibn Abbas, pointing to Muawiyah: They give water and honey to drink, and the family of so-and-so give milk to drink, while you give nabidh to drink — is it out of miserliness in you, or out of need? He said: Neither miserliness nor need is in us; rather the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us with Usamah ibn Zayd riding behind him, so we gave him of this nabidh to drink, and he drank from it and said: Do likewise."
"12946","12911 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated, from Amir al-Ahwal, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended Hajj, so a woman said to her husband: Take me for Hajj along with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said to her: I have nothing with which to take you for Hajj. She said: Take me for Hajj upon your camel so-and-so. He said: That one is confined in the path of Allah. She said: Take me for Hajj upon your water-carrying camel. He said: That one you and I take turns upon. She said: Then sell your fruit produce. He said: That is my provision and yours. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned, she sent her husband to him, saying: Convey to him peace and the mercy of Allah, and ask him what equals a Hajj performed with him. So he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my wife conveys to you peace and the mercy of Allah, and she had asked me for Hajj with you, so I said: I have nothing with which to take you for Hajj. She said: Take me for Hajj upon your camel so-and-so. I said: That one is confined in the path of Allah. He said: Had you taken her for Hajj upon it, it would have been in the path of Allah. She said: Then take me for Hajj upon your water camel. I said: That one you and I take turns upon. She said: Then sell your fruit produce. I said: That is my provision and yours. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed at her eagerness for Hajj. He said: She has charged me to ask you what suffices in place of a Hajj with you? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Convey to her peace and the mercy of Allah, and inform her that an Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj performed with me."
"12947","12912 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan informed us, (H). And Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated — both saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Ayyub and Asim and Abd al-Hamid, the companion of al-Ziyadi, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, he said: Ibn Abbas addressed us on a day of mud, and when the caller reached: Come to prayer — he ordered him to call out: Prayer in the dwellings. Some of them looked at one another, so he said: As though you disapprove of this? One better than me did this — and it is a binding obligation."
"12948","12913 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith: that Ibn Abbas ordered his caller on a rainy day, saying: When you reach: Come to success — say: Pray in the dwellings. It was said: What is this? He said: The deed of one who is better than me."
"12949","12914 - Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu al-Jumahir Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated, Said ibn Bashir narrated, from Qatadah, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say upon the pulpit: Al-Khidr was only called al-Khidr because he sat upon a white fleece and it shook forth green. Said ibn Bashir said: And Suwayd Abu Hatim related to me that Qatadah used to raise this hadith to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12950","12915 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Imran ibn Hudayr, Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq narrated, he said: Ibn Abbas was addressing one evening when a man said: The prayer! He said: May you lose your mother — do you teach us its time? We used to combine the two prayers in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12951","12916 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, he said: Ibn Abbas addressed us one day after Asr until the sun set and the stars appeared, and the people began calling to him: The prayer! Among the people was a man of Tamim calling out, so Ibn Abbas said: Do you teach me the Sunnah, may you lose your mother? I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combine Zuhr with Asr, and Maghrib with Isha. Then I met Abu Hurayrah and he agreed with him."
"12952","12917 - Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban al-Balkhi narrated, Safwan ibn Isa al-Zuhri narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Harun, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Abu Nahik, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It is of the Sunnah that when a man sits, he removes his sandals and places them beside him."
"12953","12918 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Sadaqah ibn Ubadah ibn Nashit narrated, he said: I heard my father Ubadah ibn Nashit say: I heard Ibn Abbas being asked about tila (boiled grape drink). Ibn Abbas said: I do not know what this tila of yours is that you bring; but we used to be brought something like camel tar, and we would drink it and see no harm in it."
"12954","12919 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from Abu al-Sawwar al-Sulami, from Abu Hadir, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped at al-Qahah while in ihram."
"12955","12920 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ali ibn Hujr narrated, Yusuf ibn al-Ghariq narrated, from Sukayn ibn Abi Siraj, from al-Mughirah ibn Suwayd, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Of a man's felicity is the lightness of his two jaws."
"12956","12921 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Umar ibn Salih ibn Janzah al-Wasiti narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Atiyyah narrated, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes a handspan of Mecca without right, it is as though he took it from beneath the Foot of the Most Merciful; and whoever takes anything of the rest of the land without right will come on the Day of Resurrection with it hung as a collar upon his neck from seven earths."
"12957","12922 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Ismah ibn Sulayman al-Khazzaz narrated, Sallam al-Tawil narrated, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: I do not look into the right of My servant until My servant looks into My right."
"12958","12923 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Jawshan, my father related to me: that Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of the earthen jar."
"12959","12924 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Habib ibn Shihab, my father related to me, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none among the people like a man who takes hold of his horse's head, striving in the path of Allah and restraining his harm from the people; and like a man dwelling in comfort who honors his guest and gives his due."
"12960","12925 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Muawiyah ibn Ghallab, from al-Hakam ibn al-Araj: that he came to Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was pillowing his cloak in the Sacred Mosque, and asked him about fasting the day of Ashura. He said: When you see the crescent of Muharram, count; and when it is the ninth day, wake up fasting. I said: Is that how Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast? He said: That is how Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast."
"12961","12926 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Layth, from Abu Jahdam, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me, for Satan does not take my likeness."
"12962","12927 - Yusuf the judge narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan, from Anas ibn Sulaym al-Jahdami, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: What are these reports spread among the people saying: Whoever circumambulates the House has become released? He said: That is the practice of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), even if it displeases you."
"12963","12928 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas — and more than one — from al-Hasan, he said: When the verse of debt was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first to deny was Adam, the first to deny was Adam, the first to deny was Adam. When Allah, mighty and majestic, created him, He wiped his back and brought forth his offspring and all that would scatter forth until the Day of Resurrection, and began presenting them to him. He saw among them a radiant man and said: O Lord, which of my sons is this? He said: This is your son Dawud. He said: O Lord, how long is his life? He said: Sixty years. He said: O Lord, add to his life. He said: No, unless you add to him from your own life — and Adam's life was a thousand years — so he granted him forty years of his life. He said: So a writ was written against him for that, and the angels were made witnesses over him. When Adam was dying, the angels came to take him, and he said: Forty years of my life remain. They said: You granted them to your son Dawud. He said: I did not do it, I granted him nothing. So Allah sent down the writ, and the angels bore witness against him; thus Allah completed for Adam a thousand years, and completed for Dawud a hundred years."
"12964","12929 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Jibril (peace be upon him) said: Prayer has been made beloved to you, so take from it as much as you wish."
"12965","12930 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Surat al-Anam was sent down all at once in Mecca at night, with seventy thousand angels around it chanting glorification."
"12966","12931 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas: that a man came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and said: A woman came to me to pledge allegiance, so I took her into the inner chamber, laid my hand upon her, solicited her, and did everything with her short of intercourse. Umar said to him: Woe to you — perhaps she is one whose husband is absent. He said: Yes. He said: Go to Abu Bakr and ask him. So he went to him and said to him what he had said to Umar, and he said: Woe to you — perhaps she is one whose husband is absent. Then he went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said to him the like of what he had said to Abu Bakr and Umar, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Woe to you — perhaps she is one whose husband is absent in the path of Allah. He said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent, and the Quran was sent down: {And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the approaches of the night} to the end of the verse. The man said: O Messenger of Allah, is it for me in particular or for the people in general? Umar raised his hand and struck his chest, saying: No by Allah, nor any honor to you — but for the people in general. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed and said: Umar has spoken the truth."
"12967","12932 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah drowned Pharaoh, he said: I believe that there is no god but the One in whom the Children of Israel believe — so Jibril (peace be upon him) said: O Muhammad, had you seen me while I was taking of the sea mud and stuffing it into his mouth, fearing that mercy would reach him."
"12968","12933 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none of the children of Adam but has erred or intended an error — except Yahya ibn Zakariyya."
"12969","12934 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Isbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated, (H). And Zakariyya ibn Hamdawayh al-Saffar narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated — both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us with Usamah ibn Zayd riding behind him, so we gave him of this drink to drink — meaning the drink of the watering place — and he said: You have done well; do likewise."
"12970","12935 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafii narrated, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: We recited it in the lifetime of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for two years: {And those who do not call upon another god with Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, nor commit adultery} — the verse; then there was sent down: {Except whoever repents}. And I never saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rejoice with a joy more intense than his joy over it, and over: {Indeed We have granted you a clear victory}."
"12971","12936 - Zakariyya ibn Hamdawayh al-Saffar narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated, (H). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us — both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated — both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When Uthman ibn Mazun died — then he mentioned the hadith."
"12972","12937 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ubayd Allah al-Ghaylani narrated, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated, al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House upon his mount, touching the Corner with his staff."
"12973","12938 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Imran narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated, Abu Asim al-Abbadani narrated, Ali ibn Zayd narrated, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: We were in a circle in the mosque discussing the virtues of the prophets — which of them is most excellent? We mentioned Nuh and the length of his worship of his Lord, we mentioned Ibrahim, the close friend of the Most Merciful, we mentioned Musa, the one spoken to by Allah, we mentioned Isa son of Maryam, and we mentioned the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). While we were thus, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: What are you discussing among yourselves? We said: O Messenger of Allah, we were discussing the virtues of the prophets — which of them is most excellent. We mentioned Nuh and the length of his worship, we mentioned Ibrahim, the close friend of the Most Merciful, we mentioned Musa, the one spoken to by the Most Merciful, we mentioned Isa son of Maryam, and we mentioned you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Whom did you prefer? We said: We preferred you, O Messenger of Allah — Allah sent you to all mankind, forgave you what preceded of your sin and what followed, and you are the seal of the prophets. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yet it is not fitting for anyone to say: I am better than Yahya ibn Zakariyya. We said: O Messenger of Allah, whence is that? He said: Have you not heard how Allah described him in the Quran? He said: {O Yahya, take the Book with strength, and We gave him wisdom as a child} — and he recited until he reached: {And a master, and chaste, and a prophet among the righteous} — he never did an evil deed at all, nor ever intended one."
"12974","12939 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Bukhari narrated, Ali ibn al-Hakam ibn Zibyan al-Ansari narrated, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no son of Adam but in his head is a bridle in the hand of an angel; when he is humble it is said to the angel: Raise his bridle, and when he is proud it is said to the angel: Lower his bridle."
"12975","12940 - Al-Hasan ibn Allawayh al-Qattan narrated to us, Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated, (H). And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated — both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was visited, in what the sleeper sees, by two angels; one of them sat at his feet and the other at his head. The one at his feet said to the one at his head: Strike a parable of this man and of his nation. He said: The parable of this man and of his nation is like that of traveling people who reached the edge of a desert, having neither provision to cross it nor wherewith to return; while they were thus, a man came to them wearing a Yemeni figured robe and said: If I bring you to lush meadows and full watering-places, will you follow me? They said: Yes. So he set out with them and brought them to lush meadows and full watering-places, and they ate and drank and grew fat. Then he said to them: Did I not find you in that state? They said: Yes. So you pledged that if I bring you to lush meadows and full watering-places you would follow me? They said: Yes. Then a party of them said: He has spoken the truth — by Allah, we shall surely follow him; and a party of them said: We are content with this — we shall stay here."
"12976","12941 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani and Abu Zurah al-Dimashqi narrated to us — both saying: Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated, Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, concerning: {The heart did not lie about what it saw} — he said: He saw his Lord, mighty and majestic, with his heart."
"12977","12942 - Sahl ibn Musa narrated to us, Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated, Isa ibn Shuayb narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leads a blind man until he brings him to safety, Allah, exalted be He, forgives him forty major sins — and four grave sins that entail the Fire."
"12978","12943 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated, from Abu al-Sawwar al-Sulami, from Abu Hadir, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped at al-Qahah while in ihram."
"12979","12944 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained in Mecca thirteen years receiving revelation, and in Medina ten years, and he died at sixty-three years of age."
"12980","12945 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Mihran narrated, Imran ibn Tammam narrated, Abu Jamrah Nasr ibn Imran narrated, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out saying: Of the overturning of religion is the perusal of the Nabateans and their taking palaces in the cities."
"12981","12946 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Hilal ibn Bishr narrated, Imran ibn Tammam narrated, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear turbans, you will increase in forbearance."
"12982","12947 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated, Umar ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated, Abu Jamrah Nasr ibn Imran narrated, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to a clan of the Arabs calling them to Islam, but they did not accept the letter; they returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Had I sent it to a people on the shore of Oman, of Azd Shanuah, and Aslam, they would have accepted it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to al-Julanda calling him to Islam, so he accepted it and became Muslim, and he sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a gift. It arrived after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had passed away, so Abu Bakr made the gift an inheritance and divided it among Fatimah and the people."
"12983","12948 - Ismail ibn Qirat al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, Umar ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated, Abu Jamrah narrated, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Four hundred men of Daws came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Welcome to the finest of people in faces, the sweetest of them in mouths, and the greatest of them in trustworthiness."
"12984","12949 - Yusuf the judge and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us — both saying: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, (H). And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Hakam narrated — Amr ibn Marzuq said: And Shubah informed us, while Amr ibn Hakam said: Shubah narrated, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas: that when the delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Who are the people? They said: Rabiah. He said: Welcome to the delegation — neither disgraced nor regretful. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a clan of Rabiah, we come to you from a distant land, and this clan of the disbelievers of Mudar stands between us and you, and we can only reach you in a sacred month. So command us with a decisive matter to which you call and to which we shall call those behind us, and by which we shall enter Paradise. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I command you with four and forbid you four: I command you to believe in Allah — the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Do you know what faith is? The testimony that there is no god but Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakat, the fasting of Ramadan, and that you give a fifth of the spoils; and I forbid you four: gourds, green glazed jars, hollowed stumps, and tar-coated vessels — he said: and sometimes he said: pitched vessels — memorize them and call those behind you to them."
"12985","12950 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal and Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, (H). And Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Shihab ibn Abbad al-Abdi narrated — all saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Abu Jamrah, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, this clan of Rabiah has been barred from you by the disbelievers of Mudar, so we can only reach you in a sacred month. Command us with a matter we shall hold to and call those behind us to. He said: I command you with four and forbid you four: Belief in Allah — the testimony that there is no god but Allah — and he clenched his hand — and the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakat, the fasting of Ramadan, and that you render a fifth of what you gain as spoils; and I forbid you gourds, hollowed stumps, green glazed jars, and tar-coated vessels."
"12986","12951 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us — both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gourds, tar-coated vessels, hollowed stumps, and green glazed jars."
"12987","12952 - Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Abu Mashar al-Barra narrated, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, Abu Jamrah narrated, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, between us and you are the disbelievers of Mudar, and we can only reach you in the sacred months. Command us with a matter we shall confine ourselves to and call those behind us to. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four and four: the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakat, the fasting of Ramadan, and a fifth of what you gain as spoils; and I forbid you nabidh of gourds, green glazed jars, hollowed stumps, and tar-coated vessels."
"12988","12953 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abbad ibn Abbad narrated, Abu Jamrah narrated, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we of this clan of Rabiah have been barred from you by the disbelievers of Mudar, and we can only reach you in a sacred month. Command us with a matter we shall act upon and call those behind us to. He said: I command you with four and forbid you four: Faith — and he explained it to them — the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakat, and that you render a fifth of what you gain as spoils; and I forbid you gourds, green glazed jars, hollowed stumps, and pitched vessels."
"12989","12954 - Umar ibn Hafs ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Mamar al-Muqad narrated, Abd al-Warith narrated, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas: that the delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: Welcome to the delegation. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a clan of Rabiah, and between us and you are the disbelievers of Mudar, and we can only reach you in a sacred month. Command us with a matter we shall hold to and call those behind us to. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I command you with one matter and forbid you four: Belief in Allah — the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakat, and that you render a fifth of what you gain as spoils; and I forbid you gourds, hollowed stumps, green glazed jars, and tar-coated vessels."
"12990","12955 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Anbar al-Basri narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Muadh narrated, my father narrated, Bistam ibn Muslim narrated, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas: that the delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, between us and you are the disbelievers of Mudar, and we cannot come to you whenever we wish. Inform us what is lawful for us of what is unlawful to us. He said: I command you with four and forbid you four: that you establish prayer, give zakat, fast Ramadan, and give a fifth of the spoils; and I forbid you gourds, green glazed jars, hollowed stumps, and tar-coated vessels."
"12991","12956 - Yusuf ibn Yaqub the judge narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, (H). And Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Ziyadi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated — both saying: Abu Hilal narrated, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas: that the delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, between us and you are the disbelievers of Mudar, and we can only reach you in a sacred month. Command us with what is lawful for us of what is unlawful to us. He said: I command you with one matter and forbid you four: I command you with the testimony that there is no god but Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakat, the fasting of Ramadan, and that you give a fifth of what you gain as spoils; and I forbid you gourds, green glazed jars, hollowed stumps, and tar-coated vessels."
"12992","12957 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated, Yahya ibn Adam narrated, Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, from Muhammad ibn Salamah ibn Abi Hafsah, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The first Friday gathering held after the Friday gathering of Medina was a Friday gathering in Bahrain, in a village of Abd al-Qays called Juwatha."
"12993","12958 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Isbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas: The first Friday gathering held in Medina, then the Friday gathering of Juwatha."
"12994","12959 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn Said al-Qasir narrated, Abu Jamrah narrated: that Ibn Abbas informed them of the beginning of Abu Dharr's Islam, saying: When it reached him that a man had appeared in Mecca claiming to be a prophet, he sent his brother, saying: Go to Mecca until you hear from him and bring me his news. So his brother set out for Mecca, heard of the tidings of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and returned to Abu Dharr, informing him that he commands good, forbids evil, and commands noble character. He said: You have not satisfied me. Then he took a waterskin containing water and a small vessel, then set out until he came to Mecca, fearing to ask anyone about anything, and he did not meet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until night covered him. When darkness fell, Ali ibn Abi Talib passed by him and said: Who is the man? He said: A man of Ghifar — then go to your dwelling. So he took him to his dwelling, neither of them asking his companion about anything. In the morning he went out early but did not meet him, so he stood aside in the mosque; then Ali ibn Abi Talib passed by him and said: Is it not time for the man to know his lodging? So he took him along, neither asking the other about anything. On the third day he bound Ali: if he informs him of what he seeks, he will conceal it for him and shield him — so he did. He said: It has reached me that a man has appeared in Mecca claiming to be a prophet, so I sent my brother but he brought me nothing satisfying; so I have come myself to learn his tidings. Ali ibn Abi Talib said: Follow my tracks — if I see something I fear for you from, I shall stand as though urinating and return to you; and if I see nothing, then follow my tracks. So Ali went out early and Abu Dharr followed upon his tracks until they entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he informed him of his tidings and heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: O Messenger of Allah, command me with your command. He said: Return to your people until my news reaches you. He said: No by Allah, I shall not return until I proclaim Islam. So he went out to the mosque and called out the prayer, saying: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. The polytheists said: The man has apostatized, the man has apostatized — and they beat him until he fell. Al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib passed by him and threw himself over him, then said: O company of Quraysh, you are traders and your route passes through Ghifar — do you wish the road to be cut off from you? So they held back from him. On the second day he returned to the like of his saying, so they beat him; then al-Abbas passed over him and said to them the like of that, so they held back from him. Such was the beginning of Islam for Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"12995","12960 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Matar ibn Tahman al-Warraq, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection."
"12996","12961 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Jannad narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated, from Amr ibn Ubayd, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Jibril (peace be upon him) came to me when three days remained of Dhu al-Qadah and said: Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection. At that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I foreseen of my affair what I now look back upon, I would not have driven the sacrificial animals."
"12997","12962 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, Shubah informed us, from Abu Jamrah, he said: I performed tamattu, but some people forbade me, so I asked Ibn Abbas and he commanded me with it. Then I saw in a dream as though a speaker saying: An accepted Hajj and an accepted Umrah. So I related it to Ibn Abbas and he said: Allah is Most Great — the practice of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — or he said: The practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12998","12963 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Shubah narrated, from Abu Jamrah, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: A red velvet cloth was placed in the grave of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12999","12964 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Hakam narrated, Shubah narrated, from Abu Jamrah, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray thirteen units at night."
"13000","12965 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Hakam narrated, Shubah narrated, from Abu Jamrah, he said: I said to him: Did you hear Ibn Abbas say anything about the temporary marriage with women? He said: I heard him permit it. Then a freedman of his said to him: Temporary marriage was only when the people were in need and women were few. Ibn Abbas said to him: You have spoken the truth."
"13001","12966 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mualla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated, Amr ibn al-Musawir al-Ataki narrated, Abu Jamrah narrated, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Do not seek a need from a blind man, nor seek it at night; and when you seek a need, face the man with your face, for modesty lies in the two eyes; and seek your need early in the morning, for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless my nation in its early hours."
"13002","12967 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir, Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib, and Abu Shuayb ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us — all saying: Affan ibn Muslim narrated, Hammam narrated, from Abu Jamrah, he said: I used to push back the crowd from Ibn Abbas, then I was kept from him for some days, so he said to me: What kept you? I said: Fever. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fever is of the blast of Hell, so cool it with the water of Zamzam."
"13003","12968 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Thawab ibn Utbah narrated, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Muhammad ibn Maslamah a sword and said: Fight the polytheists as long as they are fought; but when you see two swords differing among the Muslims, strike until it breaks, then sit in your house until a decisive death comes to you or an erring hand."
"13004","12969 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us — both saying: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ashajj Abd al-Qays: In you are two traits which Allah loves: forbearance and deliberation."
"13005","12970 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Allaf narrated, Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated, Shubayl ibn Azrah narrated, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of the people of the East are Abd al-Qays."
"13006","12971 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated, Ibrahim ibn al-Nadr narrated, from Hajjaj al-Aishi, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the disputant of whoever wrongs Abd al-Qays."
"13007","12972 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated, Ibrahim ibn al-Nadr narrated, from Ibrahim al-Aishi, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive Abd al-Qays — three times."
"13008","12973 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi narrated, Yazid ibn Zayd Abu Khalid narrated, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive Abd al-Qays — three times."
"13009","12974 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated, Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Abbas, he said: Al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): This is a day in which whoever controls his hearing, his sight, and his tongue will be forgiven."
"13010","12975 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ghalib narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Abu al-Nadr al-Madini, from Ziyad, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on the day Sad ibn Muadh died, stood over his grave, then said: We belong to Allah and to Him we return — then said: Had anyone been saved from the pressure of the grave, Sad would have been saved; it indeed pressed him, then it was eased from him."
"13011","12976 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, from Haywah ibn Shurayh, Malik ibn al-Khayr al-Ziyadi narrated: that Malik ibn Sad al-Tujibi related to him: that he heard Ibn Abbas say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Jibril (peace be upon him) came to me and said: O Muhammad, Allah has cursed wine, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its drinker, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its seller, its buyer, its pourer, and the one for whom it is poured."
"13012","12977 - Tahir ibn Isa ibn Qayras al-Misri narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh, al-Layth ibn Sad, and Ibn Lahiah informed me, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Thabit ibn Yazid al-Khawlani, he informed him: that he came to Medina and met Ibn Abbas and asked him about wine. He said: I shall inform you about wine. I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque; while he was sitting with his knees drawn up, he released his sitting posture, then said: Whoever has any wine with him, let him inform me of it. So the people began coming to him — one saying: I have a waterskin, another saying: I have a waterskin, another saying: I have skins and whatever Allah willed that he had. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gather it at such-and-such a graveyard, then inform me. So he rose and I rose with him; I walked at his right while he leaned upon me. Then Abu Bakr caught up with us, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took me and placed me at his left, placing Abu Bakr in my stead. Then Umar ibn al-Khattab caught up with us, so he took him and placed him at his left, and he walked between them until he stood over the wine. He said to the people: Do you know what this is? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, this is wine. He said: You have spoken the truth. Allah has cursed wine, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its drinker, its pourer, and the eater of its price. Then he called for a knife and said: Sharpen it. So they did. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it and tore open the skins. The people said: These skins have some use in them. He said: Yes — but I do this only out of anger for Allah, because of what of His wrath is in it. He said: And some of them add to others in the hadith."
"13013","12978 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth related to me, from Bakr ibn Mudar, from Jafar ibn Rabiah, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Walah al-Sabai: that he said to Abd Allah ibn Abbas: We raid the West — what do you think of their waterskins? Ibn Abbas said: There is no harm in them. I said: From your own opinion, or from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Rather, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13014","12979 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated, Jafar ibn Rabiah narrated: that he heard Abu al-Khayr informing, from Ibn Walah: that he asked Ibn Abbas, saying: We raid this West, whose people are idolaters, and they have skins in which there are milk and water. Ibn Abbas said: Tanning is purification. Ibn Walah said: From your opinion, or something you heard? He said: Rather, something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13015","12980 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Ibn Lahiah informed us, al-Harith ibn Yazid related to me, from Abu Hamzah al-Khawlani, from Ibn Abbas: that Umar ibn al-Khattab said to al-Abbas and to al-Fadl ibn Abbas: Mention to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he allot to you from the charities — and I shall attend for you. So al-Fadl mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Be patient with yourselves, O Banu Hashim, for charities are but the washings of the people."
"13016","12981 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Said Ufayr narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Ibn Hubayrah, from Amr ibn Hurayth: that Ibn Abbas — then he mentioned it."
"13017","12982 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sufyan narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Abu Qabil: that Ibn Mawhab informed him: that he was with Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan when Marwan entered upon him and spoke to him of his needs, saying: Fulfill my need, O Commander of the Faithful, for by Allah my burden is great — I have become a father of ten, a brother of ten, and an uncle of ten. When Marwan turned away, with Ibn Abbas sitting with Muawiyah upon his couch, Muawiyah said: I adjure you by Allah, O Ibn Abbas, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Banu al-Hakam reach thirty men, they will take Allah's signs among them as spoils, His servants as chattels, and His Book as deceit; and when they reach four hundred and ninety-nine, their destruction will be swifter than the fruit? Ibn Abbas said: O Allah, yes. Then Marwan mentioned a need of his, and Marwan sent Abd al-Malik back to Muawiyah to speak to him of it; when he turned away, Muawiyah said: I adjure you by Allah, O Ibn Abbas, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned this — he said: The father of the four tyrants? Ibn Abbas said: O Allah, yes. For that reason Muawiyah claimed Ziyad."
"13018","12983 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Yazid ibn Habib, from Amir ibn Yahya, from Hanash al-Sanani, from Ibn Abbas: that some people of Himyar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him about things, and a man of them said: I love women, and I love to come to my wife from behind — what do you think of that? So Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: {Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish}. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Come to her facing forward and facing backward, as long as that is in the private part."
"13019","12984 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr and Amr ibn Khalid narrated — both saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from Hanash ibn Abd Allah al-Sanani, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was born on Monday; on Monday he left Mecca and entered Medina on Monday; he conquered Badr on Monday; Surat al-Maidah was sent down on Monday: {This day I have perfected for you your religion}; he raised the Corner on Monday; and he passed away on Monday."
"13020","12985 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Yahya ibn Ayyub related to me, from Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from Hanash al-Sanani, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam is three hundred and thirteen laws — there is none of them with which its bearer meets Allah but he enters Paradise by it."
"13021","12986 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, Abd Allah ibn Hubayrah narrated, from Hanash, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the urine of camels and their milk is a cure for those whose bellies suffer looseness."
"13022","12987 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Hubayrah, from al-Araj, from Hanash, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out and pour forth water, then wipe himself with dust. So I would say: O Messenger of Allah, water is near you — and he would say: Perhaps I shall not reach it."
"13023","12988 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth related to me, from Qays ibn al-Hajjaj, from Hanash al-Sanani, from Ibn Abbas: that he was behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to me while I was riding behind him: O boy, I shall teach you some words — guard them: Guard Allah and He will guard you; guard Allah and you will find Him before you; when you ask, ask Allah; when you seek help, seek help from Allah; and know that were the nation to gather to benefit you, they would not benefit you except with something Allah has already written for you. The pens have dried and the pages have been folded."
"13024","12989 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Abu Sadaqah al-Qaratisi Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala narrated, Nafi ibn Yazid informed us, Qays ibn al-Hajjaj informed me, from Hanash al-Sanani: that he heard Abd Allah ibn Abbas say: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — then he mentioned the like of the hadith of al-Layth ibn Sad."
"13025","12990 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin ibn al-Misri narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated, Salih ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Baylamani, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Marry off the unmarried women — three times — upon whatever the families agree, even a handful of arak wood."
"13026","12991 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth ibn Sad related to me, from Said ibn Bashir, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Baylamani, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever says in the morning: {So glory be to Allah when you enter evening and when you enter morning. And to Him belongs praise in the heavens and the earth, and at nightfall and when you enter noon} — the whole verse — attains what he missed in his day; and whoever says it in the evening attains what he missed of his night."
"13027","12992 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Ibn Hubayrah, from Alqamah ibn Walah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: What is Saba — a man, or a woman, or a land? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man who begot ten; six settled in Yemen and four in Syria. As for the Yemenis: Madhhij, Kindah, al-Azd, the Ashariyyun, Anmar, and Himyar. As for the Syrians: Lakhm, Judham, Amilah, and Ghassan."
"13028","12993 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Jubarah ibn Mughallis narrated, al-Hajjaj ibn Tamim al-Jazari narrated, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not guide you to a word that saves you from associating partners with Allah? {Say: O you disbelievers} — at your bedtime."
"13029","12994 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated, Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every taloned bird and every fanged beast of prey."
"13030","12995 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Abu Bishr, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every fanged beast of prey and every taloned bird."
"13031","12996 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ubayd Allah al-Ghaylani narrated, Abu Qutaybah narrated, Shubah narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every fanged beast of prey."
"13032","12997 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Imran ibn Zayd narrated, al-Hajjaj ibn Tamim narrated, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Abd Allah ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There shall be a people at the end of time called al-Rafidah who reject Islam and cast it off — so kill them, for they are polytheists."
"13033","12998 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi and Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us — both saying: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated, al-Hajjaj ibn Tamim narrated, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Ali was with him, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ali, there shall be in my nation a people professing love of us, the People of the House; they have a nickname — they are called al-Rafidah. So kill them, for they are polytheists."
"13034","12999 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muawiyah al-Naysaburi narrated, Abu al-Malih narrated, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes perform ghusl on Friday and sometimes leave it."
"13035","13000 - Jafar ibn Ahmad al-Shami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Ubayd ibn Muhammad narrated, from Sabbah ibn Yahya al-Muzani, from Abu Fazarah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was not commanded to decorate the mosques."
"13036","13001 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated, from Layth, from Abu Fazarah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was not commanded to decorate the mosques."
"13037","13002 - Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Hammad al-Barbari narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Layth, from Abu Fazarah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas — raised: I was not commanded to decorate the mosques."
"13038","13003 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated, my father narrated, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated, from Abu Fazarah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was not commanded to decorate the mosques — and he did not mention Layth."
"13039","13004 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated, from Abu Shihab al-Hannat, from Layth, from Abu Fazarah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things — whoever lacks even one of them, Allah forgives him what is besides that for whom He wills: whoever dies not associating anything with Allah, who is not a sorcerer following sorcerers, and who bears no rancor against his brother."
"13040","13005 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-Ajlah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What Allah wills and what you will. He said: You have set up a rival to Allah — rather, what Allah alone wills."
"13041","13006 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, from al-Ajlah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What Allah wills and what you will. He said: You have made me an equal — say: What Allah wills."
"13042","13007 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Jafar ibn Burqan narrated, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm: that the lizard was mentioned before Abd Allah ibn Abbas, and one of his companions said: It was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), yet he neither permitted it nor forbade it. Ibn Abbas said: Evil is what you say. Umm Hufayd, the daughter of al-Harith, came visiting her sister Maymunah, the daughter of al-Harith, with food containing lizard meat. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came after dusk had fallen — meaning darkness — so Maymunah said: O Messenger of Allah, it is lizard meat. So he refrained from it, and Maymunah refrained from it. Ibn Abbas said: Those with him ate it — and had it been forbidden he would have forbidden them from it. And he said: It is not in our land, and we find it distasteful."
"13043","13008 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, Sulayman al-Shaybani narrated, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, he said: A man invited us and brought us thirteen lizards. In the morning I came to Ibn Abbas and mentioned that to him, and his companions spoke much about it, until one of them said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I neither permit it nor forbid it. Ibn Abbas said: Evil is what you have said. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was only sent making lawful and making unlawful. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at Maymunah's, with al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas, Khalid ibn al-Walid, a woman, and Maymunah with him; a tray was brought with bread and lizard meat upon it. He withheld his hand and said: This is meat I have never eaten — but eat. So Khalid ibn al-Walid, al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas, and the woman ate. Maymunah said: I shall not eat food from which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has not eaten — so Maymunah did not eat."
"13044","13009 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Sufyan al-Thawri informed us, from al-Shaybani, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas: that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, shall I perform Hajj on behalf of my father? He said: Yes — if you do not add good to him, you will not add evil to him."
"13045","13010 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Awn al-Kharraz narrated, Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated, Abd al-Jalil ibn Atiyyah narrated, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Truffles are of the manna, and their water is a cure for the eye."
"13046","13011 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, (H). And Muhammad ibn al-Rabi ibn Shahin narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated — both saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, he said: Ibn Abbas said: Any man who claims kinship to other than his parents, or takes as patrons other than his freedmen who freed him — upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels until the Day of Resurrection; neither requital nor ransom shall be accepted from him."
"13047","13012 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Abbas, he said: A band of Jews once attended the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Abu al-Qasim, inform us of traits we shall ask you of, which none knows but a prophet. He said: Ask me of whatever you wish — but grant me the covenant of Allah and what Yaqub took upon his sons: that if I inform you of something and you recognize it, you will follow me. He said: That is yours. He said: Four traits we ask you of — inform us: Which food did Israil forbid himself before the Torah was sent down? Inform us how the woman's fluid is from the man's fluid, and how the female and the male come from it? Inform us how this unlettered Prophet is among the people, and who is his patron among the angels? He said: Then upon you is the covenant of Allah — that if I inform you, you will follow me. So they gave him whatever covenant and pact he wished. He said: I adjure you by the One who sent down the Torah upon Musa — do you know that Israil fell gravely ill, his sickness grew long, and he vowed: if Allah cured him of his sickness, he would surely forbid the most beloved drink and the most beloved food to him — and the most beloved food to him was camel meat, and the most beloved drink to him was their milk? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness over them. He said: I adjure you by Allah, besides whom there is no god — do you know that the man's fluid is thick and the woman's fluid is thin and yellow, and whichever of the two prevails, the child and the resemblance are by Allah's permission: if the man's fluid prevails it is a male by Allah's permission, and if the woman's fluid prevails it is a female by Allah's permission? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness over them. He said: I adjure you by the One who sent down the Torah upon Musa — do you know that this unlettered Prophet's eyes sleep while his heart does not sleep? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness over them. They said: Now you — inform us who is your patron among the angels, for upon that we shall join you or part from you. He said: My patron is Jibril (peace be upon him) — and Allah, mighty and majestic, never sent a prophet but he was his patron. They said: Upon that we part from you — had your patron been other than him among the angels, we would have followed you and believed you. He said: What prevents you from believing him? They said: He is our enemy. Thereupon Allah, mighty and majestic, said: {Whoever is an enemy to Jibril — for he brought it down upon your heart by Allah's permission, confirming what was before it, and guidance and glad tidings for the believers. Whoever is an enemy to Allah} up to: {Behind their backs, as though they do not know}. Thereupon they returned with anger upon anger."
"13048","13013 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, he said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was forbidden women except what was of the believing emigrant women. He said: {It is not lawful for you to marry women after this} — the verse — up to His saying: {And a believing woman if she offers herself to the Prophet}. And He forbade every woman of a religion other than Islam. He said: {And whoever disbelieves in faith, his deed has perished} — the verse: {O Prophet, We have made lawful for you your wives} up to His saying to the believers — and He forbade what is besides that of the kinds of women. Yet Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah married a Jewess, and Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman married a Christian woman, so Umar grew wrathful with intense anger, nearly assaulting them both. They said: We shall divorce, so do not be angry. Umar said: If their divorce is lawful, then their marriage was lawful — but we shall surely wrest them away, pale and withered."
"13049","Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a slaughtered animal be hamstrung before it dies."
"13050","13014 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated, Abd Allah ibn Abbas related to me: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to a woman of his people called Sawdah — she was one with many children, having five or six young ones by a husband of hers who had died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: What prevents you from me? She said: By Allah, O Prophet of Allah, nothing prevents me from you except that you are the most beloved of creation to me, yet I honor you too much for these young ones to cry out at your head morning and evening. He said: Does anything besides that prevent you from me? She said: No, by Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: May Allah have mercy on you — the best women to ride the rumps of camels are the righteous women of Quraysh: the most tender toward a child in his infancy, and the most heedful toward a husband in his means."
"13051","13015 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, Utbah ibn Abi Hakim reported to me, Shahr ibn Hawshab reported to me, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever drinks wine is impure for forty days; if he repents from it, Allah turns to him in forgiveness; if he goes back, he goes back to impurity; if he repents, Allah turns to him; if he goes back, he goes back to impurity for forty days; if he repents from it, Allah turns to him; but if he does it a fourth time, it becomes binding upon Allah to give him to drink from the discharge of al-Khabal. They said: O Abu al-Abbas, what is the discharge of al-Khabal? He said: The fat of the people of the Fire and their pus."
"13052","13016 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Tarif narrated, al-Qasim ibn Malik narrated, from Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rakahs in which he recited the Mother of the Book and did not add anything to them."
"13053","Muslim ibn al-Muhriz from Ibn Abbas. 13017 - Abu Zayd al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Thalabah ibn Muslim al-Khathami, from Muslim ibn Abi al-Muhriz, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He commanded five things and forbade ten: he commanded parting the hair of the head, the siwak, trimming the mustache, sniffing water, and rinsing the mouth; and he forbade that a woman be married together with her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt, or that two women gather in one garment, and forbade shighar, and forbade the sale of dogs, the dowry of the prostitute, the earnings of the cupper, the skins of predatory animals, wearing qassi garments, and the stud fee of the stallion."
"13054","Umm Uthman from Ibn Abbas. 13018 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muslim ibn Sallam narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Umm Uthman, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no shaving upon women; upon women is only shortening."
"13055","13019 - Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Saigh narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Had, Hind bint al-Harith al-Khathamiyyah, the wife of Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, reported to me, from Umm al-Fadl and Abd Allah ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he stood one night at Makkah in the night and said: O Allah, have I conveyed, three times. So Umar ibn al-Khattab stood, and he was tender-hearted, and said: O Allah, yes; you were eager and strove and advised; O Allah, yes; you were eager and strove and advised. Then in the morning he said: Faith shall surely prevail until it drives disbelief back to its homelands, and the seas shall surely be crossed with Islam, and there shall surely come upon the people a time in which they learn the Quran and teach it and recite it, then they say: We have recited and learned, so who is better than us? Is there any good in such people? They said: No, O Messenger of Allah. And who are they? He said: They are from among you, and they are the fuel of the Fire."
"13056","Ali ibn Abi Talhah from Ibn Abbas. 13020 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated, from Ali ibn Talhah, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: {And they ask you about the orphans; say: setting right for them is best}. That was before there was sent down: {Those who consume the wealth of the orphans unjustly only consume fire in their bellies, and they shall roast in a blaze}. The Muslims disliked eating with the orphans and were scrupulous about mixing with them in anything, so they asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: {Say: setting right for them is best; and if you mix with them, they are your brothers; and Allah knows the corrupter from the reformer; and had Allah willed, He would have put you in hardship}. That is, He would have constrained you, but He widened and eased; then He said: {And whoever is rich, let him abstain, and whoever is poor, let him eat in a fair manner}. That is, the poor guardian, when he manages the orphan's wealth, eats according to his standing over his wealth and its benefit, so long as he does not waste."
"13057","13021 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Muawiyah ibn Salih reported to me, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: {And when you are among them and establish the prayer for them, let a party of them stand with you}. This is the prayer at fear: the imam stands, and a party of them stands with him, while a party take their weapons and stand facing the enemy; the imam prays one rakah with those with him, then he remains sitting in his posture, and they stand and pray the second rakah by themselves while the imam is sitting; then they leave until they reach their companions and stand in their station; then the others come forward, and the imam prays the second rakah for them. Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with the people on the day of Batn Nakhlah."
"13058","13022 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Muawiyah ibn Salih reported to me, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: {There is no blame upon you in seeking bounty from your Lord}. That is, there is no harm upon you in buying and selling before entering ihram and after it. As for the ihram, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that one marry, or marry off, or slaughter until he finishes his ihram."
"13059","13023 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Muawiyah ibn Salih reported to me, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: {Those who avoid the major sins and shameful deeds}. He said: The greatest of the major sins is associating partners with Allah, because Allah said: {Whoever associates partners with Allah, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him}; and despairing of the mercy of Allah, for Allah said: {None despairs of the mercy of Allah except the disbelieving people}; and feeling secure from the plan of Allah, for Allah, mighty and majestic, says: {None feels secure from the plan of Allah except the losing people}; and among them is disobedience to parents, for Allah, mighty and majestic, made the disobedient one overbearing, wretched; and killing the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, for Allah, blessed and exalted, says: {His recompense is Hell}, the verse; and slandering chaste women, for Allah, majestic in His mention, says: {They are cursed in this world and the Hereafter, and for them is a great punishment}; and consuming the wealth of the orphan, for Allah, mighty and majestic, says: {They only consume fire in their bellies, and they shall roast in a blaze}; and fleeing from battle, for Allah, exalted, says: {And whoever turns his back to them on that day, except as a maneuver for battle or joining a company, has returned with anger from Allah, and his abode is Hell, an evil destination}; and consuming usury, for Allah, exalted, says: {Those who consume usury do not stand except as stands the one whom Satan has confounded with touch}; and sorcery, for Allah, exalted, says: {And they knew that whoever buys it has no share in the Hereafter}; and adultery, for Allah says: {He shall meet punishment; multiplied for him is the punishment on the Day of Resurrection, and he shall abide therein humiliated}; and the immersing false oath, for Allah says: {Those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price}, the verse; and misappropriation of spoils, for Allah, exalted, says: {And whoever misappropriates shall bring what he misappropriated on the Day of Resurrection}; and withholding the obligatory zakah, for Allah, exalted, said: {With them shall be branded their foreheads, their sides, and their backs}; and false testimony, for Allah, mighty and majestic, says: {And whoever conceals it, his heart is sinful}; and drinking wine, for Allah, mighty and majestic, equated it with idols; and deliberately abandoning the prayer or anything of what Allah has made obligatory, for the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: Whoever abandons the prayer deliberately is free of the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger; and breaking the covenant, and severing kinship."
"13060","13024 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Muawiyah ibn Salih reported to me, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prompt your dead with the testimony that there is no god but Allah; whoever says it at his death, Paradise becomes binding for him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what of one who says it in health? He said: That is even more binding, even more binding. Then he said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if the heavens and the earths were brought, and those in them and what is between them and what is beneath them, and placed in one scale of the balance, and the testimony that there is no god but Allah were placed in the other scale, it would outweigh them."
"13061","13025 - Bakr narrated to us, Abd Allah narrated, Muawiyah narrated, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ibn Abbas, regarding: {Among them are wretched and happy}, and the like of this in the Quran. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was eager that all the people believe and follow him upon guidance, so Allah informed him that none believes except one for whom happiness preceded in the first Decree, and none strays except one for whom wretchedness preceded in the first Decree. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, said to His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): {Perhaps you will kill yourself that they are not believers}. That is: {If We will, We send down upon them a sign from heaven, so their necks remain bowed to it}."
"13062","13026 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Muawiyah ibn Salih reported to me, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: {Say: I do not ask you for any reward except love for kinship}. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had kinship in all of Quraysh; when they denied him and refused to follow him, he said: O my people, if you refuse to follow me, then preserve my kinship among you, and let no others among the Arabs be more worthy of protecting me and aiding me than you."
"13063","13027 - Bakr narrated to us, Abd Allah narrated, Muawiyah reported to me, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: {Those who, when a calamity befalls them, say: We belong to Allah and to Him we return; upon them are blessings from their Lord and mercy, and they are the guided}. He said: Allah, mighty and majestic, informed us that when the believer submits to the decree of Allah and returns, and says the return-to-Allah formula at calamity, three traits of good are recorded: blessing, mercy, and the realization of the path of guidance. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says the return-to-Allah formula at calamity, Allah mends his calamity, makes his outcome good, and grants him a righteous successor with whom he is pleased."
"13064","13028 - Bakr narrated to us, Abd Allah narrated, Muawiyah reported to me, from Ali, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: {That they may increase in faith along with their faith}. He said: Allah, mighty and majestic, sent His Prophet with the testimony that there is no god but Allah; when they affirmed it, He added for them the pilgrimage; when they affirmed it, He added for them jihad; then He completed their religion for them, and said: {Today I have completed for you your religion and perfected upon you My favor}. Ibn Abbas said: The firmest, truest, and most complete faith of the inhabitants of the heavens and the earth is the testimony that there is no god but Allah."
"13065","13029 - Bakr narrated to us, Abd Allah narrated, Muawiyah ibn Salih reported to me, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: {And do not recite loudly in your prayer nor whisper in it}. He says: One should not pray showing off to people, nor abandon it for fear of people."
"13066","13030 - Bakr narrated to us, Abd Allah narrated, Muawiyah ibn Salih reported to me, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: {And it is a reminder for you and your people}. He said: An honor for you and your people."
"13067","13031 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Muawiyah ibn Salih reported to me, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: {And remember the favor of Allah upon you and His covenant with which He bound you when you said: We hear and obey; and fear Allah; Allah is Knowing of what is in the breasts}. That is, when Allah sent the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sent down upon him the Book, they said: We believe in the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and in the Book, and we affirm what is in the Torah. So Allah reminded them of His covenant which they acknowledged upon themselves, and commanded them to fulfill it."
"13068","13032 - Bakr narrated to us, Abd Allah narrated, Muawiyah reported to me, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: {The recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger and spread corruption in the land}. He said: They were a people of the People of the Book between whom and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) there was a covenant and pact; they broke the covenant and spread corruption in the land, so Allah gave His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a choice: if he wished, to kill, and if he wished, to crucify, and if he wished, to cut their hands and feet from opposite sides. As for banishment, it is flight in the land; if he comes repentant and enters Islam, it is accepted from him, and he is not taken for what preceded from him."
"13069","13033 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah narrated, Muawiyah ibn Salih reported to me, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: {If you are given this, take it, and if you are not given it, beware}. They are the Jews: a woman among them committed adultery, and Allah, mighty and majestic, had ruled in the Torah that in adultery there is stoning. They grudged stoning them both and said: Go to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); perhaps he has a concession, so accept it. They came to him and said: O Abu al-Qasim, a woman among us committed adultery; what do you say about her? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How did Allah rule in the Torah regarding adultery? They said: Leave the Torah; what do you have regarding that? He said: Bring me your most knowledgeable of the Torah that was sent down to Musa (peace be upon him). Then he said to them: By the One Who saved you from the household of Pharaoh, and by the One Who split the sea and saved you and drowned the household of Pharaoh, inform me of what Allah ruled in the Torah regarding adultery. They said: He ruled with stoning."
"13070","774 - Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with them both: mention of his age and death. 13034 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar, surnamed Abu Abd al-Rahman, died at Makkah after the pilgrimage and was buried at al-Muhassab; some people say at Fakhkh. His age, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted him on the day of the Trench for combat, was fifteen years; the Trench was in Shawwal of year four; his age on the day he died was eighty-four."
"13071","13035 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi al-Tahhan al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, from Malik ibn Anas, he said: Ibn Umar remained after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sixty years, with delegations of people coming to him."
"13072","13036 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, from Malik ibn Anas, he said: Ibn Umar remained after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sixty years, with delegations of people coming to him."
"13073","13037 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Abu Zayd ibn Abi al-Ghimr, whose name is Abd al-Rahman, narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from Malik ibn Anas, he said: The age of Ibn Umar on the day he died was eighty-four."
"13074","13038 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Madini Fustuqah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated, from al-Waqidi, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar died in year seventy-four and was buried at Fakhkh, at eighty-four years of age."
"13075","13039 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated, from Atiyyah, he said: I said to a freedman of Ibn Umar: How was the death of Ibn Umar? He said: The ferrule of a man of the people of Syria struck him in his foot. Al-Hajjaj came to him visiting him and said: If I knew who struck you, I would strike his neck. He said: It is you who struck me. He said: How? He said: The day you brought weapons into the sanctuary of Allah."
"13076","13040 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Suwayd al-Zari narrated, Umarah ibn Zad han narrated, Makhul reported to me, he said: While I was with Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, as he was walking, a black man carrying a spear passed by him, and the ferrule of the spear landed between the forefinger and thumb of Ibn Umar's foot. The old man was carried and taken inside, and his leg swelled. Al-Hajjaj came to him visiting him and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, who struck you with this, so that I may take your due from him? He said: By Allah, will you take from him? He said: By Allah, I shall take your due from him. He said: How is it that weapons are carried in the sanctuary and security of Allah? He said: Then he died of it."
"13077","13041 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: My father brought me on the day of Uhud to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I was fourteen, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not permit me. Then he brought me on the day of the Trench when I was fifteen, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned a stipend for me. Nafi said: It was reported to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, and he ordered that a stipend be assigned only to one of fifteen years."
"13078","13042 - Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar informed me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I was presented to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I was fourteen years old. Then he mentioned the like of the report of Abd Allah ibn Umar, except that he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz would not assign a stipend to anyone until he reached puberty, except one hundred dirhams, and he would not assign a stipend to a newborn until weaned. While he was circling one night at the prayer place, a boy cried, and he said to his mother: Nurse him. She said: The Commander of the Believers does not assign a stipend to a newborn until weaned, and I have weaned him. Umar said: I almost killed him; nurse him, for the Commander of the Believers shall assign for him. Then after that he assigned for the newborn when born."
"13079","13043 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, from Ibn Jabir, Sulayman ibn Musa reported to me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that he would enliven the night with prayer, then say: O Nafi, has dawn come? He would say: No. Then he would resume prayer, then say: O Nafi, has dawn come? I would say: Yes. Then he would sit and seek forgiveness and supplicate until morning."
"13080","13044 - Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I have not eaten to satiety since I accepted Islam."
"13081","13045 - Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran al-Naqid narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated, from Burd ibn Sinan, from Nafi, he said: Ibn Umar would distribute in a single sitting thirty thousand, yet a month would not pass upon him in which he ate a morsel of meat in it. Burd said: I said to Nafi: Did he eat meat? He said: When he fasted or traveled, that was most of his food."
"13082","13046 - al-Hasan ibn Alluyah al-Qattan narrated to us, Ismail ibn Isa al-Attar narrated, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated, from Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Jafar ibn al-Harith, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, he said: A man came to Ibn Umar and said: What prevents you from this affair, when you are the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the son of the Commander of the Believers? He said: What prevents me from it is that Allah, mighty and majestic, has forbidden to me the blood of my Muslim brother. He said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: {And fight them until there is no trial and the religion is all for Allah}. Ibn Umar said: We fought them until there was no trial and the religion was all for Allah, while you want me to fight until there is trial and the religion is for other than Allah."
"13083","13047 - Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Hammad al-Barbari narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated, Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated, from Layth, from Nafi, he said: When Uthman was killed, Ali came to Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: You are beloved among the people, so go to Syria. Ibn Umar said: By my kinship, and my companionship of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the kinship between us - and he did not repeat it to him."
"13084","13048 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, al-Mutim ibn al-Miqdam al-Sanani reported to me, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf wrote to Abd Allah ibn Umar: It has reached me that you sought the caliphate, and the caliphate suits not one who is tongue-tied, nor miserly, nor jealous. Ibn Umar wrote to him: As for what you mentioned of the caliphate, that I sought it - I did not seek it, and it is not on my mind. As for what you mentioned of tongue-tiedness, miserliness, and jealousy: whoever has gathered the Book of Allah is not tongue-tied; whoever pays the zakah of his wealth is not miserly; and as for what you mentioned of jealousy, the worthiest thing I am jealous over is my child, that another share him with me."
"13085","13049 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Hanash, he said: I saw upon Abd Allah ibn Umar two Maafiri garments, and his garment reached half the shin."
"13086","13050 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin: that khazz shawls were gifted to Ibn Umar, among them a red shawl, and he divided them among his sons."
"13087","13051 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Yunus ibn Abi Yafur narrated, from his father, he said: I heard Ibn Umar, when a man asked him: What clothes shall I wear? He said: What the foolish do not despise you in, nor the wise find fault with you in. He said: What is it? He said: Between five dirhams and twenty dirhams."
"13088","13052 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, who heard Mujahid reporting from Ibn Umar: that when he intended that a man accompany him on a journey, he stipulated upon him that he not accompany him upon a dung-eating camel, nor dispute with us the call to prayer, nor fast except with our permission."
"13089","13053 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, he said: Nafi said: A man would accompany Ibn Umar on travel, and he ordered us to wake him and prepare his pre-dawn meal for him."
"13090","13054 - Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Saigh narrated to us, Abu Musab narrated, Abd Allah ibn al-Harith al-Jumahi narrated, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated, he said: Ibn Umar passed by a shepherd of sheep and said: O shepherd of sheep, is there a slaughter animal? The shepherd said: Its master is not here. Ibn Umar said: Say: The wolf ate it. The shepherd raised his head to the sky, then said: Then where is Allah? So Ibn Umar bought the shepherd and bought the sheep, freed him, and gave him the sheep."
"13091","13055 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, he said: When Abd Allah ibn Umar met Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he would say: Peace upon you, O son of the one with two wings."
"13092","13056 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, Ayyub narrated, from Muhammad: that Ibn Umar was asked about musk, and he said: Is it not your finest perfume?"
"13093","13057 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Ayyub narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sirin: that Ibn Umar saw a man supplicating with two fingers, so he closed one of his fingers and said: {Allah is only one God}."
"13094","13058 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Abu Mijlaz, he said: I would ask Ibn Umar at the House about the witr, and he kept saying: The end of the night. I said: What do you think, what do you think? He said: Put your what-do-you-think by that star - and he pointed to the sky - the night prayer is two by two, and the witr is one rakah at the end of the night."
"13095","13059 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Yahya al-Bakka, he said: A man said to Ibn Umar: I love you for Allah. Ibn Umar said: But I hate you for Allah. He said: Why? He said: You embellish in your call to prayer, and you take a wage for it."
"13096","13060 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Yahya al-Bakka, he said: Ibn Umar saw a storyteller telling stories in the Sacred Mosque, with a son of his with him. His son said to him: What is this one saying? He said: This one says: Know me, know me."
"13097","13061 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, Ziyad ibn Mikhraq narrated, Hammad Hifzi narrated, from Taylasah ibn Ali, from Ibn Umar, he said: People never exchanged among themselves anything better than lending for breeding: a man lends his mare and its reward flows for him, a man lends his stallion and its reward flows for him, and a man lends his ram and its reward flows for him."
"13098","13062 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, he said: I was sitting with Ibn Umar when a man asked him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I have entered ihram and gathered my hair. He said: Did you not hear Umar in his caliphate say: Whoever braids his head or mats it, let him shave? He said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I did not braid it, but I gathered it. Ibn Umar said: A she-goat and a he-goat, a he-goat for a she-goat."
"13099","13063 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from Salim, from his father, he said: The believer is not a vilifier nor a curser. He said: And I never heard Ibn Umar curse anyone at all except one man."
"13100","13064 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Muadh narrated, my father narrated, Ibn Awn narrated, from Muhammad, he said: Garlic would be crushed for Ibn Umar and strung on a thread, cast into the broth on a thread, and drawn out on a thread, then discarded, and he would eat."
"13101","13065 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Muadh narrated, my father narrated, Ibn Awn narrated, from Muhammad, he said: Ibn Umar said: The finest food, which is picked out from the molars, weakens the molars."
"13102","13066 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated, Abu Asim narrated, from Qurrah, he said: I said to Ibn Sirin: Did they joke? He said: They were but like people; Ibn Umar would joke and recite poetry, and he would say:"
"13103","13067 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi: that Ibn Umar fell ill, and a bunch of grapes was bought for him for a dirham. A beggar came, and he said: Give it to him. A man went against it and bought it from him for a dirham, then brought it to him; the beggar came asking, and he said: Give it to him. A man went against it to him and bought it from him for a dirham; he wanted to return until he was prevented. Had Ibn Umar known of that bunch, he would not have tasted it."
"13104","13068 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that he would enter the bathhouse, and the bathhouse keeper would apply depilatory to him; when it reached his waist, he would say to the bathhouse keeper: Go out."
"13105","13069 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated, Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated, from his father, he said: I entered upon Abd Allah ibn Umar while a slave girl was shaving hair from him, and he said: Depilatory thins the skin."
"13106","13070 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated, from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, from Nafi: that when Ibn Umar bathed, he would open his eyes and insert his fingers into his navel."
"13107","13071 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Ata ibn Yaqub, he said: Ibn Umar borrowed from me a thousand dirhams, and he repaid me with better than them. I said to him: Your dirhams are better than mine. He said: Whatever excess is in them is a gift to you from me."
"13108","13072 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Yazid ibn Kaysan al-Yashkuri, from Abu Hazim: that Ibn Umar passed by a man with some small sheep of his and said to him: For how much do you sell these sheep of yours? He said: For such and such. Ibn Umar said: I take them for such and such. He swore he would not sell them. Ibn Umar went on and relieved himself, then passed by him, and he said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, take them for what you offered me. He said: You swore an oath, and I would not aid Satan against you by making you break it."
"13109","13073 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated, from al-Amash, from Abu Hazim, he said: We bought a house from Ibn Umar, and he sat at the door and much dust rose. We said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, we take only what is right, and we do not deceive you. He said: I fear suspicion."
"13110","13074 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father reported to me, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Umar ibn Nafi, from his father: that when Ibn Umar prayed alone in the days of tashriq, he would not say the takbir after the prayer."
"13111","13075 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Warkani narrated, Jarir narrated, from al-Amash, from Nafi, he said: Ibn Umar stayed with a people; when three days had passed, he said: O Nafi, spend upon us from our wealth, for we have no need to be given charity."
"13112","13076 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father reported to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated, Shubah narrated, from Sufyan, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Muawiyah, from Ibn Umar: that he used to recite this lettering: {When we are decayed bones}."
"13113","13077 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Musa ibn Tharwan, from Abu al-Mutawakkil: that he saw Ibn Umar with his waist-wrapper to half his shin, his shirt above that, and his cloak above the shirt."
"13114","13078 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, he said: I saw Ibn Umar hastening between the two عرضs, saying: I am for it, I am for it."
"13115","13079 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Husayn, from Abd Allah ibn Sabrah, he said: When Ibn Umar woke in the morning, he would say: O Allah, make me of the greatest of Your servants in share of every good You apportion in the morning, and light You guide with, and mercy You spread, and provision You extend, and harm You remove, and affliction You lift, and trial You turn away."
"13116","13080 - al-Haytham ibn Khalaf al-Duri narrated to us, Muammal ibn Hisham narrated, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated, from al-Sari ibn Yahya, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: Ibn Umar would sometimes break his fast upon intercourse."
"13117","And of what Abd Allah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, transmitted in marfu form. Ibn Abbas from Ibn Umar. 13081 - al-Hasan ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Qarani narrated, Abu Shihab narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I was at a funeral, and Ibn Umar was with it. He heard weeping, and Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The dead is punished by the weeping of his family over him."
"13118","Tariq ibn Shihab from Ibn Umar. 13082 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Shabab al-Usfuri reported to me, Sahl Abu Attab narrated, Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a sick man of his Companions, and I was with him. He entered upon him while he was praying upon a stick, placing his forehead upon the stick. He gestured to him, so he threw the stick and took a cushion. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave it from you; if you are able to prostrate upon the ground, otherwise gesture with a gesture, and make your prostration lower than your bowing."
"13119","13083 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid al-Dimashqi narrated, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated, from Umar ibn Dharr, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab: that he met Ibn Umar as a pilgrim or umrah-performer. I came to him and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, we are people of a land where we hire white land for dinars and dirhams. He said: We dislike that; this is muhaqalah. I said: Then we give land for a third or a fourth. He said: There is no harm in that; we used to do that."
"13120","Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah from Ibn Umar. 13084 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rashid reported to me, Abd Allah ibn Jafar narrated, from Maslamah ibn Abi Maryam, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever's intercession stands in the way of a hadd of the hadds of Allah has opposed Allah in His command."
"13121","Said ibn al-Musayyib from Ibn Umar. 13085 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Yahya ibn Said, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Umar, he said: When we missed a man at Fajr and Isha, we thought ill of him."
"13122","13086 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father reported to me (ha). And Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated, both saying: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated, Shubah narrated, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, he said: I heard Salim ibn Razin reporting from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), regarding a man who has a wife, then divorces her, then another man marries her and divorces her before consummating with her - is she lawful for the first? He said: No, until she tastes the little honey. Abu al-Qasim said: Shubah erred in this report in two places: his saying from Salim ibn Razin, when it is Sulayman ibn Razin; and he added Said ibn al-Musayyib in the chain. Sufyan al-Thawri and Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated it from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Razin al-Ahmar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and that is the correct one."
"13123","13087 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dead is punished for what is wailed over him."
"13124","13088 - Yusuf al-Qadi and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, both saying: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shubah informed, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"13125","13089 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Uthman al-Shami narrated, al-Dahhak ibn Hamzah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Refrain from the people of la ilaha illa Allah; do not declare them disbelievers for a sin. Whoever declares the people of la ilaha illa Allah disbelievers is himself closer to disbelief."
"13126","13090 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated (ha). And Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, both saying: al-Harith ibn Ubayd Abu Qudamah narrated, Hud ibn Shihab ibn Abbad al-Asari narrated, from his father, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Umar, he said: I performed Hajj with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with Abu Bakr, and with Umar, and with Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them - all of them would not fast it, meaning the day of Arafah."
"13127","13091 - Ahmad ibn Ziyad al-Araj al-Iyadi narrated to us, Bajilah, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Muan ibn Rifah, from al-Asamm, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever mutilates his brother, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Al-Asamm means Yazid ibn Hurmuz, and Allah knows best."
"13128","13092 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated, Rishdin ibn Sad narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sahm, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the fear prayer with these one rakah and with these one rakah."
"13129","13093 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Wuhayb narrated (ha). And Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated (ha). And Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated, all of them from Abd al-Khaliq ibn Salamah al-Shaybani, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, he said: I heard Ibn Umar say: A delegation of Abd al-Qays came with al-Ashajj and asked the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about drink. He said: Do not drink in hantamah, nor in dubba, nor in naqir."
"13130","13094 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Hammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, Idris al-Awdi narrated, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, he said: I attended Ibn Umar at a funeral; when he placed it in the lahd, he said: In the name of Allah, and in the path of Allah, and upon the creed of the Messenger of Allah. When the bricks were taken to the lahd, he said: O Allah, protect her from Satan and from the punishment of the grave. When they leveled the heap over her, he stood beside the grave, then said: O Allah, keep the earth from her sides, raise her spirit, and grant her Your pleasure. I said: Are these things you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or things you said from your opinion? He said: Then I am able to speak; rather, I heard them from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13131","al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Ibn Umar. 13095 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated (ha). And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, from Amr ibn al-Harith, that Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim reported to him, from his father, from Ibn Umar: that he used to report from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The sun and the moon are not eclipsed for anyone's death nor life, but they are two signs of the signs of Allah; when you see them, pray."
"13132","13096 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim reported to him, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The night prayer is two by two; when you wish to leave, bow one which makes odd what you prayed."
"13133","13097 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys food shall not sell it until he takes full possession of it."
"13134","13098 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from al-Mundhir ibn Ubayd al-Madini, that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad reported to him, that Abd Allah ibn Umar reported to him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling food bought by measure until he takes full possession of it."
"13135","13099 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one in ihram shall not wear the shirt, nor the qabas, nor trousers, nor the turban, nor cloaks with hoods, nor anything touched by saffron or wars."
"13136","13100 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Ali ibn Hujr al-Marwazi narrated, al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Muwaqqari narrated, from al-Zuhri, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you are white garments; wear them, and shroud your dead in them."
"13137","13101 - Abu Hanifah Muhammad ibn Hanifah al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar narrated, Anas ibn Iyad narrated, from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two traders have the choice so long as they have not parted."
"13138","13102 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jafar ibn Humayd narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Umar, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey; it was a dark night; the caller of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the adhan and prayed, then he ordered a crier to call out: Pray in your dwellings."
"13139","13103 - And with its chain, from Ibn Umar, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey; it was a dark night; the caller of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the adhan and prayed, then he ordered a crier to call out: Pray in your dwellings."
"13140","13104 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Hamid ibn Yahya narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two shall not converse privately to the exclusion of a third."
"13141","Salim from Ibn Umar. 13105 - Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated, my brother reported to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ibn Abi Atiq, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim: that Abd Allah ibn Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: People are but like a hundred camels; one can hardly find among them a riding camel."
"13142","13106 - Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Salimi narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways al-Asha narrated, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Abi Atiq and Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls."
"13143","13107 - Salamah ibn Ahmad al-Fawzi al-Himsi narrated to us, my grandfather Khattab ibn Uthman al-Fawzi narrated, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated, Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when travel pressed him on a journey, delay Maghrib until he joined it with the Isha prayer."
"13144","13108 - Salamah ibn Ahmad al-Fawzi al-Himsi narrated to us, my grandfather Khattab ibn Uthman al-Fawzi narrated, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated, Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever misses the Asr prayer, it is as if his family and wealth were taken from him."
"13145","13109 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) obligated, for rain-fed and river-irrigated land, the tenth, and for what is watered by drawing, half the tenth."
"13146","13110 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated, Attab ibn Bashir narrated, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Salim and Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman: that Abd Allah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Isha at the end of his life; when he gave the salam, he said: Have you seen this night of yours? For at the head of a hundred years, none of those upon the earth shall remain."
"13147","13111 - Salamah ibn Ahmad al-Fawzi al-Himsi narrated to us, my grandfather Khattab ibn Uthman al-Fawzi narrated, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated, Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) begin the takbir in prayer and raise his hands until he placed them level with his shoulders; then when he said the takbir for bowing, he did the like of that. Then he said: Allah hears one who praises Him, and did the like of that. Then he said: Our Lord, to You is praise, and did the like of that."
"13148","13112 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Haywil, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he said the takbir in prayer, would raise his hands level with his shoulders; when he bowed, he did the like of that; when he raised his head, he did the like of that; and when he said: Allah hears one who praises Him, he said: Our Lord, to You is praise, and did the like of that - and he would not do so in prostration."
"13149","13113 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Sufyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Amr ibn Qust narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Allah hears one who praises Him; our Lord, and to You is praise. Then he would say before prostrating: O Allah, curse so-and-so and so-and-so. Then he would say the takbir and prostrate, until Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: {You have nothing of the affair}."
"13150","13114 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Sufyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Amr ibn Qust narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the fear prayer with one party one rakah, while the other party faced the enemy. Then they left and stood in the station of their companions, facing the enemy, and those others came, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them one rakah. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the salam; then these made up one rakah and those one rakah."
"13151","13115 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed, Mamar informed, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned the like of it."
"13152","13116 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from Ibn Umar: that he prayed it with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the like of it."
"13153","13117 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, al-Ala ibn Sulayman narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from what fire has touched."
"13154","13118 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, al-Ala ibn Sulayman narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution."
"13155","13119 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man look at the private parts of his brother."
"13156","13120 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade praying upon the middle of the road, or relieving oneself upon it, or urinating in it."
"13157","13121 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abd al-Qahir ibn Rishdin ibn Sad narrated, my father narrated, from Qurrah and Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another."
"13158","13122 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated, Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of one sitting is like half the prayer of one standing."
"13159","13123 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi al-Misri, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, saying: Abu Musab narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two rakahs of Fajr: {Say: O disbelievers} and {Say: He is Allah, One}."
"13160","13124 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Jafar ibn Rabiah, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: Neither the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor Abu Bakr, nor Umar would wear rings, nor seal a letter, until Ziyad ibn Abi Sufyan wrote to Umar ibn al-Khattab: You write to us things that have no seals. At that he took a ring, and with it letters were sealed."
"13161","13125 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Habib the scribe of Malik narrated, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, the nephew of al-Zuhri, narrated, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever honors me regarding my Companions shall come to my Pond, and whoever does not honor me regarding my Companions shall not see me on the Day of Resurrection except from afar."
"13162","13126 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruits until they begin to turn yellow or red."
"13163","13127 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw upon Umar a white shirt and said: Is this shirt of yours new or washed? He said: Rather washed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear new, live praised, die a martyr, and may Allah grant you the coolness of eyes in this world and the Hereafter. He said: And you too, O Messenger of Allah."
"13164","13128 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Tamim al-Sulami narrated, al-Zuhri reported to me, from Salim: that Abd Allah ibn Umar said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when travel hurried him on a journey, delay the Maghrib prayer until he joined it with the Isha prayer."
"13165","13129 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Tamim narrated, al-Zuhri narrated, Salim reported to me, from Abd Allah ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would glorify Allah while upon his mount, not caring in which direction it faced."
"13166","13130 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Ali ibn Mabad narrated, Khalid ibn Sinan narrated, Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sells date-palms after they have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates; and whoever sells a slave who has wealth, his wealth belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates."
"13167","13131 - Ahmad ibn Shuayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasai narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh informed, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: In the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we would say: Abu Bakr, and Umar, and Uthman."
"13168","13132 - Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to us, my father narrated (ha). And Umarah ibn Wathimah ibn Musa ibn al-Furat Abu Rifah al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Salim, from al-Zubaydi, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri reported to me, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alive, we would say: The best of this ummah after its Prophet is Abu Bakr, and Umar, and Uthman. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would hear that and not disapprove. We do not know of Uthman committing any major sin, nor killing a soul without right; but it is this wealth: if he gives it to you, you are pleased, and if he gives Quraysh, you are angry. You only wish to be like Persia or Rome, who leave no ruler for them but they kill him."
"13169","13133 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father reported to me, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated, he said: I read to Ibn Jurayj, Ziyad ibn Sad narrated, that Ibn Shihab reported to him, Salim reported to me, from Ibn Umar: that he would walk in front of the funeral, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman would walk ahead of it. My father said of this report: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - it is only from al-Zuhri in mursal form; and the report of Salim is the deed of Ibn Umar; and the report of Ibn Uyaynah seems mistaken."
"13170","13134 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father reported to me, al-Abbas ibn al-Hasan narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar would walk ahead of the funeral."
"13171","13135 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Uqayl and Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar walking ahead of the funeral."
"13172","13136 - Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated, my brother reported to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Abu Atiq and Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim: that Abd Allah ibn Umar would walk ahead of the funeral, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman would walk in front of it."
"13173","13137 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated (ha). And Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated, both saying: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim; he does not wrong him nor surrender him. Whoever is engaged in the need of his brother, Allah is engaged in his need. Whoever relieves a Muslim of a distress of this world, Allah relieves him thereby of a distress of the distresses of the Day of Resurrection. And whoever covers a Muslim, Allah covers him on the Day of Resurrection."
"13174","13138 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Zamah ibn Salih narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not stung from one hole twice."
"13175","13139 - Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Saigh narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated, Sulayman ibn Bilal reported to me, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not raise your gazes to the sky, lest they be snatched - meaning in prayer."
"13176","13140 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consulted the Muslims about what would gather them for prayer. They said: The horn. He disliked it on account of the Jews. Then the bell was mentioned, and he disliked it on account of the Christians. That night the call was shown to Abd Allah ibn Zayd, a man of the Ansar, and Umar ibn al-Khattab. The Ansari knocked at the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Bilal, and he called the adhan with it."
"13177","13141 - Abu Shubayl Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Waqid narrated to us, my father narrated, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: Two men of the Ansar recited a surah which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had taught them, and they would recite with it. One night they stood praying and could not manage a letter of it. In the morning they came early to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is of what was abrogated and caused to be forgotten, so leave it. Al-Zuhri would recite it: {Whatever verse We abrogate or cause to be forgotten}, with dammah on the nun, light."
"13178","13142 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Bishr ibn Mansur narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The most frequent oaths of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were: No, by the Turner of hearts."
"13179","13143 - Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, Azhar ibn Jamil narrated, Ishaq ibn Isa, son of the daughter of Dawud Abu Hind, narrated, Zamah ibn Salih narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: No head was ever carried to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), not even on the day of Badr to Madinah."
"13180","13144 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muawiyah al-Naysaburi narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered sharpening the blades and hiding them from the animals."
"13181","13145 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Allaf narrated, Maymun ibn Zayd narrated, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from Mansur ibn Dinar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar: that he was asked about mutah, and he said: It is forbidden. It was said: Ibn Abbas sees no harm in it. He said: By Allah, Ibn Abbas knew that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it on the day of Hunayn, and we were not fornicators."
"13182","13146 - Amr ibn al-Tahir ibn Abi al-Sarh and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Qattan, the two Egyptians, narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, from al-Dahhak, from Nafi, from Salim: that he heard Abd Allah ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Ibn Sayyad while he was playing with the boys, and struck him with his foot and said: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? Ibn Sayyad said: I bear witness that you are the messenger of the unlettered. He said: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I believe in Allah and His Messenger."
"13183","13147 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Junadah ibn Salm narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I saw a black woman with disheveled head who left Madinah until she stood at Mahyaah, which is al-Juhfah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I interpreted that the fever of Madinah was moved to al-Juhfah."
"13184","13148 - And with its chain, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he passed by Ibn Sayyad while he was playing with the boys, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck him with his foot and said: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? Ibn Sayyad said: I bear witness that you are the messenger of the unlettered. Ibn Sayyad said to him: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I believe in Allah and His Messengers."
"13185","13149 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Abbadi al-Basri narrated, Muslim ibn Salim al-Juhani narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar reported to me, from Nafi, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to me as a visitor, with no need impelling him but visiting me, it becomes binding upon me to be an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"13186","13150 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Abbadi narrated, Muslim ibn Salim narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated, from Nafi, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cupping in the head is for madness, leprosy, vitiligo, drowsiness, and molar pain."
"13187","13151 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Ruzzi narrated, Asim ibn Mihja narrated, Maslamah ibn Salim narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar reported to me, Nafi reported to me, from Salim, from his father, he said: A boy came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I intend this direction, the Hajj. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked with him and said: O boy, may Allah provision you with piety, direct you to good, and suffice you worry. When the boy returned, he greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he raised his head to him and said: O boy, may He accept your Hajj, expiate your sin, and replace your expense."
"13188","13152 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: I read to Abd Allah ibn Nafi, from Asim ibn Umar, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar: that Salim informed him that his father informed him: that it was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at al-Muarras, the resting place of al-Shajarah: Ask, for it is the valley of Makkah, blessed."
"13189","13153 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Abu Bakr ibn Salim, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, Allah builds for him a house in the Fire."
"13190","13154 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Muhammad ibn Bishr and Abu Usamah narrated, both saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Salim, from his father, from his grandfather: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"13191","13155 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah ibn Umar reporting from Abu Bakr ibn Salim, from his father, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw in sleep that I was given a large bowl filled with milk; I drank from it until I was full, until I saw it flowing in my veins between the skin and the flesh. Something remained, and I gave it to Umar ibn al-Khattab. Interpret it. They said: O Prophet of Allah, this is knowledge Allah gave you and filled you with; something remained, and you gave it to Umar ibn al-Khattab. He said: You have hit right."
"13192","13156 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, he said: I said to Idris ibn Isa al-Qattan: Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi reported to you, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Salim, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: What is between my grave and my pulpit is a garden of the gardens of Paradise, and my pulpit is upon my Pond. He brought out its original and said: I wrote it from Muhammad ibn Bishr."
"13193","13157 - Salamah ibn Nahid al-Maqdisi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Utbah al-Dimashqi narrated (ha). And Mahmud ibn Ali al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Salimi narrated, both saying: Abd Allah ibn Nafi narrated, Asim ibn Umar reported to me, from Bilal ibn Abi Bakr, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every intoxicant is forbidden."
"13194","13158 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Yahya al-Tujibi narrated, from Ibn Lahiah, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A dog diminishes every day two qirats, except a harmful hunting dog or a sheepdog. Abu al-Qasim said: Diminishes, meaning from its owner's reward."
"13195","13159 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father reported to me, Ibn Lahiah narrated, Abu al-Nadr reported to me, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Of grapes there is wine, of raisins there is wine, of dates there is wine, of wheat there is wine, and I forbid every intoxicant."
"13196","13160 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn Rushdin ibn Sa'd al-Misri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, from Musa ibn Umar ibn Qudamah, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when someone died, would say: Place him before our Farat; what an excellent Farat for my Ummah is Uthman ibn Maz'un."
"13197","13161 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj narrated to him that Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to him, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill snakes; whoever finds the one with two stripes and the tail-less one and does not kill them is not of us, for they are the two that snatch sight and cause what is in the wombs of women to miscarry."
"13198","13162 - Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Waki'i narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated, Yazid ibn Iyad narrated, from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no envy except in two cases: a man whom Allah taught the Qur'an and he stands with it during the hours of the night and the hours of the day, and a man whom Allah gave wealth and he spends it during the hours of the night and the hours of the day."
"13199","13163 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Salim and Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated, both said: Waki' narrated, from Sufyan, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: The oath of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: No, by the Turner of hearts."
"13200","13164 - Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated, Wuhayb narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: The oath of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: No, by the Turner of hearts."
